&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain core components of our software delivery platform using Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an extensive suite of automated tests covering flashing workflows, mock peripherals, and gRPC contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with R&amp;amp;D and Production teams to gather technical requirements and translate them into actionable features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain robust CI/CD pipelines to guarantee reliable, efficient software deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement low-level Linux flashing pipelines for NVIDIA Jetson devices, including LUKS disk encryption and Secure Boot signing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years writing clean, tested, and concurrent Go applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of Linux foundations, such as systemd, udev rules, network interfaces, disk partitioning, and bash scripting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record writing automated tests for systems software, mocks/stubs for hardware and OS interfaces, or CI-driven integration suites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience writing CI/CD pipelines, preferably for GitLab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience integrating Go applications with GCP APIs (Cloud Storage, Secret Manager, IAM/OAuth).&lt;/li&gt;
