hroughout Germany, Austria, and Switzerland use our solution to manage reservations, table planning, guest data, and processes all in one place—smartly, efficiently, and tailored to their workflows. This leaves more time for what really matters: their guests.<br>As a working student in marketing, you’ll ensure that even more hospitality professionals learn about aleno and understand how we make their day-to-day work easier. Your ideas won’t end up in a drawer—they’ll go straight to our customers.</p><br><strong>Your responsibilities</strong><p>With us, you work on projects rather than by the book. Instead of simply ticking off tasks, you support projects and follow them through different phases, from idea to result, giving you real insight into how marketing works in a growing SaaS company.</p><br><strong>What You'll bring to the table</strong><p><ul><li>You are currently enrolled in a Bachelor's or Master's programme in Marketing, Communications or Business Administration with a focus on Marketing.</li><li>First practical experience in marketing, e.g. through an internship, a part-time job or your own projects, is a big plus.</li><li>You enjoy writing and are good at it, in German at native level and confidently in English.</li><li>You are happy to travel to trade fairs occasionally and represent aleno on site.</li><li>You work independently and in a structured way, and you like to roll up your sleeves.</li><li>A passion for gastronomy and hospitality is a particular bonus.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Why You’ll love working at aleno</strong><p><ul><li>A steep learning curve: you take something away from every project that helps you grow professionally</li><li>A real perspective: if it's a good fit for both sides, this can turn into a permanent full-time position after you graduate.</li><li>Flexible working hours that fit around your semester schedule</li><li>A modern office in Berlin Mitte and the option to work partly remotely</li><li>Insights into different areas of marketing at a growing SaaS company</li><li>A small, dedicated team where you settle in quickly, with short decision paths and plenty of room for your ideas</li><li>A monthly tax-free benefit in kind worth €50.</li><li>Discounts with numerous brands through our employee discount programme.</li><li>A MacBook as your work device.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Role details</strong><p>Location: Berlin<br>Hours: 20 hrs/week, more hours possible during semester breaks<br>Start: as soon as possible</p><br><strong>Our hiring process</strong><p>After you apply, we will always get back to you within 7 working days. If your profile matches our requirements, here's what happens next:<br><ol><li><strong>Intro call with Sophia</strong> (People &amp; Culture, approx. 30 minutes via video): We talk about you, your motivation and any questions you have about aleno.</li><li><strong>Interview with Stefan</strong> (Head of Growth, approx. 30 minutes via video): Together you dive deeper into the tasks and the areas that interest you.</li><li><strong>Decision:</strong> You will hear back from us promptly, whatever the outcome.</li></ol></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/aleno/working-student-marketing-berlin-483123","tags":[],"job_types":["Entry","Intern","Part time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1791716992},{"slug":"logistics-manager-retail-d2c-berlin-327391","company_name":"Holy","title":"Logistics Manager - Retail & D2C (m/f/d)","description":"<br><strong>About HOLY</strong><p><ul><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;"><a style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;" href="http://www.weareholy.com/"><strong style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">HOLY</strong></a><strong style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;"> is the soft drink revolution</strong>: With our product lines Energy®, Iced Tea®, Hydration®, Milkshake®, and our newest innovation, the HOLY Syrup Bottle® you get amazing taste across 50+ flavors while maintaining a good conscience—for your body &amp; the environment.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;"><strong style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">Over 2M loyal customers:</strong><span> </span>Started in a shared apartment by three best friends, we have scaled to Europe's fastest growing consumer brand—and our cult-like community, the HOLY Squad, loves it: 4.6 stars on<span> </span><a style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;" href="http://reviews.io/">reviews.io</a><span> </span>speak for themselves.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;"><strong style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">From D2C to Global Omnichannel:</strong><span> </span>In less than four years, we've profitably scaled HOLY to more than €250M D2C revenue in DACH, FR, UK and PL. Now scaling our retail business, we're on an exciting transition to becoming a true omnichannel rocketship.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;"><strong style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">We are still just getting started:</strong><span> </span>Backed by the world's best consumer investors, we aim to revolutionize the soft drink industry and build a generational love brand: tastier, healthier &amp; more sustainable. Our team of 200+ people aims high (Coca-Cola, we're coming for you!).</li></ul></p><br><strong>About the Position</strong><p>HOLY is growing fast: with new product launches, expanding retail partnerships, and an ever-increasing customer base driving demand across all channels.<br><br>To keep pace with this momentum, we are looking for a Logistics Manager with a clear focus on Retail and a strong connection to D2C Logistics. You will make sure that retail orders are prepared completely and delivered on time, while also supporting reliable D2C fulfillment, inventory flow, and customer experience.<br><br>This role is highly operational and hands-on. You are the kind of person who spots a problem, takes ownership, and fixes it before it becomes a bigger issue.<br><br><strong>Retail Logistics Ownership</strong><br><ul><li>Take end-to-end responsibility for ensuring that retail orders are complete and ready for shipment on time.</li><li>Own Retail OTIF performance and proactively steer against deviations with fulfillment partners and retail customers.</li><li>Coordinate display assembly, capacity planning, timelines, and escalations.</li></ul><br><strong>D2C Logistics Support</strong><br><ul><li>Support reliable D2C order fulfillment, inventory flow, replenishment, and delivery performance.</li><li>Monitor open operational issues and coordinate quick resolutions with fulfillment partners, Supply Chain, Customer Service, and E-Commerce.</li><li>Support accurate system synchronization across warehouses and sales channels.</li></ul><br><strong>3PL Partnership &amp; Operations Oversight</strong><br><ul><li>Act as an operational contact for our fulfillment partners across Retail and D2C topics.</li><li>Ensure SLA adherence and daily operational stability.</li><li>Escalate and resolve deviations in speed, accuracy, availability, or cost efficiency swiftly.</li></ul><br><strong>Performance Analysis &amp; Reporting</strong><br><ul><li>Track retail and D2C logistics KPIs and turn them into actionable insights.</li><li>Use partner reports and internal dashboards to identify risks, recurring issues, and improvement opportunities.</li><li>Maintain clear SOPs, documentation, and performance reporting for internal visibility.</li></ul><strong>Cross-Functional Coordination</strong><br><ul><li>Act as the communication bridge between Logistics, Inside Sales, Retail, E-Commerce, Customer Service, Supply Chain, and external partners.</li><li>Keep stakeholders informed of critical operational updates, risks, and changes.</li><li>Lead root-cause investigations and coordinate quick resolutions to protect customer experience.</li></ul><strong>Process Improvement &amp; Scalability</strong><br><ul><li>Improve recurring logistics workflows across Retail and D2C.</li><li>Identify efficiency and cost-reduction opportunities and track implementation progress.</li><li>Help build scalable logistics playbooks for HOLY's omnichannel growth.</li></ul></p><br><strong>About You</strong><p><ul><li><strong>Retail-Ops-Ownership</strong>: You take full end-to-end responsibility for retail order readiness and OTIF performance, proactively steering against deviations before they become escalations.</li><li><strong>3PL &amp; partner management</strong>: Proven experience managing fulfillment partners operationally - holding them to SLAs, resolving deviations in speed, accuracy or cost quickly and calmly.</li><li><strong>Cross-functional coordination</strong>: Comfortable acting as the bridge between Logistics, Retail, E-Commerce, Customer Service and Supply Chain, keeping stakeholders aligned even when things move fast.</li><li><strong>Analytical &amp; KPI-driven</strong>: Skilled at turning partner reports and internal dashboards into actionable insights, spotting risks and recurring issues early.</li><li><strong>Language proficiency</strong>: Fluency in English and German is a must.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Our Offering</strong><p>In today's job market, A-players have many options to choose from. As part of our offer, we prioritise providing a productive working environment and opportunities for growth. In addition to competitive compensation, including company shares, you can expect:<br><ul><li><strong>A successful and growing company:</strong> Join a company that has been growing profitable and quickly for the last 36+ months and have just raised a series B, while many other e-commerce companies are struggling.</li><li><strong>Huge impact:</strong> Enjoy huge impact to shape HOLY’s internationalisation in a top market.</li><li><strong>Awesome team:</strong> Join an awesome team of colleagues who are ambitious, funny, down-to-earth, and authentic. Get to know us and see for yourself!</li><li><strong>Top product:</strong> Marketing is important, but a good product is essential. Our differentiated soft drinks have won over customers. Check out our <a href="https://www.reviews.io/company-reviews/store/holy">reviews.io</a> reviews or contact us for free samples.</li><li><strong>Startup culture:</strong> Join a startup culture that values flat hierarchies, fast pace, and personal development. With us, you can make a real impact.</li><li><strong>Perfect setup:</strong> Enjoy a perfect setup that includes all the requirements of a modern employer, such as a central office in Berlin Prenzlauerberg, flexible working hours, and much more.</li><li><strong>Competitive comp. + equity:</strong> Join us at a pivotal stage of hypergrowth. We offer a strong salary and meaningful equity—giving you the chance to share in our current success and benefit from the massive upside as we scale.</li></ul>Find out more about HOLY and our team on our careers page.</p><br><strong>The Process</strong><p>As we are experiencing rapid growth and have ambitious plans, the optimal start date for the position is today. Nonetheless, we are prepared to patiently await the arrival of the ideal candidate, recognizing that quality ultimately yields the best results.<br><ol><li><strong>Getting to know you:</strong> After reviewing your CV, Eric, our Talent Acquisition Manager, will have a 30-minute screening interview with you to discuss more about HOLY and the position and see if our expectations match.</li><li><strong>Hiring Manager Interview with Jan:</strong> Deep dive into your experience and approach with Jan, our Senior Logistics Manager.</li><li><strong>Case study:</strong> As soon as you have successfully completed the first 2 interviews, you will receive a case study.</li><li><strong>Advanced discussion:</strong> In this on-site meeting, the team will discuss your case study with you and answer questions in our office, the HOLY Temple. Here you will also meet Markus, our COO.</li><li><strong>Founder interview:</strong> As a strong cultural fit is important to us, you will have a final meeting with Fredi, one of our HOLY founders. This gives both you and us the opportunity for a final check.</li><li><strong>Job offer and decision:</strong> If everything goes well, you will receive an offer and we are ready to embark on this journey together with you!</li></ol>Typically his process should take around 2 weeks.</p><br><strong>Any questions or concerns?</strong><p>If you have any questions or feedback, please send an email to <a style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit;" ----- -----<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/holy/logistics-manager-retail-d2c-berlin-327391","tags":[],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1791716985},{"slug":"senior-project-manager-digital-plattform-automotive-hamburg-7537","company_name":"BBDO Germany","title":"Senior Project Manager Digital Plattform Automotive (m/w/d)","description":"<br><strong>Deine Aufgaben</strong><p><strong>Über die Rolle</strong><br>Wir suchen dich als Senior Project Manager für unseren großen Kunden aus dem Automobilbereich am Standort Hamburg. Da du intern wie extern die kommunikativen Fäden in der Hand hältst und direkt mit dem Kunden am Tisch sitzt, sind fließende Deutschkenntnisse für diese Rolle deine absolute Basis. Dein Fokus liegt zu einhundert Prozent auf der Betreuung, Pflege und redaktionellen Weiterentwicklung komplexer digitaler Webplattformen. Du verantwortest den langfristigen und nachhaltigen Betrieb unserer digitalen Produkte. Als Senior bist du das strategische und organisatorische Rückgrat für unsere Content Teams sowie UX Designer und stellst sicher, dass neue Inhalte strukturiert, geprüft und pünktlich live gehen.<br><br><strong>Deine Aufgaben</strong><br>Du übernimmst die operative Ste