&lt;p&gt;When you click “Apply now” below, your information is sent to MAP/VML. To learn more about how we process your personal data during when you apply for a role with us, on how you can update your information or have the information removed please read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://wt-map.com/privacy-policy&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;1be1ea03-7c74-4825-b023-8bda1dc2d911&quot;&gt;Privacy policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. California residents should read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wundermanthompson.com/california-recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;02863cf9-cae6-4a11-b7f1-4f68ba8e0816&quot;&gt;California Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/map/ai-product-director-london-446314","tags":["Technology & Innovation"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1791723303},{"slug":"implementation-manager-uk-united-kingdom-364630","company_name":"Bobyard","title":"Implementation Manager (UK)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Bobyard</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Construction is a multi-trillion-dollar industry that still estimates by hand. Contractors measure and count materials off drawings manually, and it caps how many jobs they can bid. Bobyard uses computer vision and NLP to automate takeoffs and estimates, so contractors bid faster and win more. We raised a $35M Series A led by 8VC, with Primary and Pear, and we're growing fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own the first 45 days of every new customer, from signed contract to a live, trained, adopting account. Launch quality can't depend on whichever CSM picks it up, so this role runs one repeatable process. You win when customers launch fast and the CSM who inherits the account never has to ask what happened. This seat is remote in the UK, works UK hours alongside our San Francisco team, and supports our largest customers in the region.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn every AE/SE handoff into a confirmed launch plan within 48 hours of signature</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Configure accounts and run kickoff and hands-on training that gets crews using Bobyard on real jobs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive customers to their first completed workflow and adoption milestone inside 45 days</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run reinforcement sessions and office hours that catch stragglers before they churn</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Chase blockers with CS and Product until they're resolved, not just logged</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hand off to the CSM with every exit criterion closed and the account documented</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years owning SaaS onboarding or implementation across a real portfolio of accounts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on comfort configuring software yourself</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've run live training for non-technical or field-based users</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record against a launch or time-to-value SLA, and you know your numbers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sharp, structured written communication</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable owning 10+ concurrent launches with little day-to-day oversight</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vertical SaaS or construction tech experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CRM or onboarding tooling (Salesforce, Asana, Notion)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Built an onboarding playbook from scratch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bilingual (Spanish or otherwise)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cash for stability. Bonus for performance. Equity for ownership. Your package reflects your role, your experience, and what you deliver, and it grows as you do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">£70,000–£90,000 base (£110,000+ OTE) + equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Occasional trips to our San Francisco HQ</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full-time, remote in the UK.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Comp Philosophy </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cash for stability. Bonus for performance. Equity for ownership. Your package reflects your role, your experience, and what you deliver.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: £70K – £90K • 0.01% – 0.03% • Offers Bonus</p><ul><li> • £70K – £90K • 0.01% – 0.03% • Offers Bonus</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/bobyard/implementation-manager-uk-united-kingdom-364630","tags":["Post Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1791722408},{"slug":"associate-director-people-strategy-execution-london-153188","company_name":"Clearbank","title":"Associate Director,  People Strategy & Execution","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Associate Director, People Strategy &amp; Execution</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We built ClearBank on the belief that banking infrastructure would no longer slow down progress. Instead, it would be a catalyst that unlocks the potential to innovate. It would adapt to different needs so a new era in financial services could begin. We’re here to challenge the status quo in banking, are you?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We all know that transforming banking forever is not an easy mission, but we’re more than ready to rise to that challenge. We all do it every day; navigating new, unexpected and sometimes even daunting challenges. But we believe in ourselves and trust we can do it. Want to innovate? Go for it. Push for a better way? You Can. If you think you have it in you, this is Where You Can.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Purpose</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting to the Group Chief People Officer and sitting on the People Leadership Team, the Associate Director, People Strategy &amp; Execution plays a central role in shaping how the function operates and delivers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">They turn ClearBank’s People strategy into a focused plan and drive delivery through the People Leadership Team and programme owners. They connect priorities, programmes, budgets and governance - creating clarity, strengthening accountability and ensuring decisions lead to action and measurable outcomes. The role gives a clear view of progress, risks and investment choices, while coordinating high-quality reporting for Group ExCo, Board and TopCo.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a high-impact, hands-on role with broad exposure across ClearBank. When priorities stall or complex challenges arise, they step in to unblock progress, bring structure and pace, and lead critical programmes that matter to the business</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the People strategy and roadmap,</strong> partnering with the Group Chief People Officer and People Leadership Team to translate business priorities into clear outcomes, choices and plans.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive execution of the People roadmap through People leaders and programme owners,</strong> maintaining oversight of progress, outcomes, risks and dependencies; providing constructive challenge; resolving cross-functional blockers; and escalating issues and decisions to keep delivery on track.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead executive and Board reporting,</strong> producing clear, commercially focused insight and recommendations for Group ExCo, Board, investors and other senior forums.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead selected high-priority People initiatives,</strong> bringing structure, pace and stakeholder alignment to complex work requiring additional focus or acceleration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own People Team operations and governance,</strong> running effective forums, agendas, decisions, actions and escalations, and ensuring clear ownership and follow-through.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the People budget and Finance partnership,</strong> overseeing planning, forecasting, expenditure and investment choices to align resources with priorities and optimise costs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build portfolio and programme capability across the People function,</strong> putting in place proportionate standards, tools and ways of working that improve delivery, alongside clear management information on outcomes, costs, risks, dependencies, capacity and decisions required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve how the People function operates,</strong> using clearer standards, simpler processes, data, digital tools and AI to strengthen consistency, insight and effectiveness.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What success looks like in the role:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The People strategy is clearly articulated, understood and translated into a prioritised roadmap with</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank’s People strategy is translated into action and delivers measurable outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Group Chief People Officer has a clear, reliable view of what is being delivered, by when, and where progress is at risk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The People Leadership Team is aligned around the roadmap, decisions, ownership and delivery expectations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Capacity constraints and competing demands are visible early, with clear recommendations on priorities, sequencing and trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Issues and dependencies are surfaced and resolved quickly, keeping critical work on track.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The People function operates effectively and consistently, with proportionate governance, clear accountability and strong follow-through.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The People function is represented credibly and commercially through high-quality reporting to Group ExCo, Board, investors and other senior forums.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Skills &amp; Experience (must-have)</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Significant experience translating functional or business strategy into prioritised roadmaps and measurable outcomes.</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong programme or portfolio leadership experience</strong>, driving delivery through others using proportionate, adaptable approaches.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience building effective governance and operating rhythms</strong> across senior leadership teams and complex portfolios.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellent analytical, written and visual communication skills</strong>, turning complex information into concise, high-quality papers, presentations and recommendations for executive and Board audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong commercial and financial acumen</strong>, including budget ownership, forecasting, resource planning and investment trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Credibility and influence with senior leaders</strong>, with the judgement to challenge constructively, align stakeholders and embed decisions without formal authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A pragmatic, solutions-focused track record of simplifying complexity and improving execution</strong>, using proportionate standards, adaptable tools, data and AI to improve insight and delivery without unnecessary bureaucracy.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working within, or in close partnership with, a People or HR function.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in banking, fintech, financial services or another regulated environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supporting Group ExCo, Board, or investor governance forums.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience operating across multiple countries, legal entities or a matrix organisational structure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with OKRs or comparable strategy execution methodologies.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ways of Working &amp; Culture</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build trust together:</strong> Own outcomes end to end, follow through on commitments and create transparency around progress, risks and decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Care like we mean it:</strong> Consider the impact of strategic and operational decisions on colleagues, clients and the organisation, while providing direct and respectful challenge.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow with the challenge:</strong> Remain resilient in a fast-moving environment, simplify complexity and use feedback and evidence to continually improve plans and delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Succeed as one:</strong> Engage stakeholders early, bring teams together around shared priorities and put organisation-wide outcomes ahead of functional boundaries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear a bold new path:</strong> Challenge legacy approaches, convert ideas into practical action and build governance and delivery solutions that can scale.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>If this sounds like you, then we encourage you to dust off that CV and apply!</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>*Please note that we are not currently able to sponsor applicants for immigration purposes.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A little bit more about us!</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ClearBank is Where You Can belong:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At ClearBank we think about Diversity, Equity and Inclusion (DE&amp;I) a lot. Not because we think we should. But because we know we should – how else can we build a happy workforce and be successful as a business. We’re committed to making sure our teams reflect society. And we put energy and effort into making this a place where everyone feels at home, where they’re given the trust and encouragement to do their very best work. Here are some of the things we’re most proud of: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">42% of our senior management roles are held by women </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our enhanced family leave policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launching our partnership with Code First Girls </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Increasing awareness of neurodiversity in the workplace through our partnership with the Inclusive Group </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our hiring process and what you can expect:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application:</strong> a member of our talent acquisition team will review your application against the key requirements for the role and let you know within two weeks whether you’re moving forward to the next stage; </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Screening:</strong> You’ll spend 30-45 minutes speaking to one of our recruiters learning more about the role and ClearBank, and we’ll get it know more about you, your experience and how your skills align with the role (this will be via phone or Teams video call). You can expect to hear back from us within seven days following this meeting (if things are taking longer than expected, we’ll let you know that too); </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Interview:</strong> You’ll spend one hour with a member of our hiring team focusing on your skills, competencies and your ways of working at the same time we’ll give you time to ask more questions about the role, the team and learn more about the ClearBank culture. This will be via Teams.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Second Interview:</strong> This will be a competency-based interview with one or more members of our team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final Stage: </strong>You will have a final meeting with the Head of Department. This will be around 45-60 minutes.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offer:</strong> Congratulations! Get ready to transform banking forever! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our commitment to you as a candidate:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We will always try our best to get back to you within seven days of your interview whether you’ve been successful or not and provide you with feedback. Sometimes things take a little longer, so we may not have a decision to share but we will get it touch to let you know we need a little more time.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re unable to provide specific individual feedback at the application or screening stage but know that your application was reviewed and considered carefully.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We wish you the best of luck with your application and maybe we’ll be celebrating your new role at ClearBank soon!  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank is committed to ensuring equal opportunities throughout every stage of the recruitment process. ClearBank recognises that diversity is vital to the long-term success of the business in the communities and markets in which it operates. ClearBank is also a firm believer that an inclusive culture fosters greater employee engagement and collaboration. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank strives for diversity and inclusion of all forms, including (but not limited to): gender, age, educational and professional background, disability, gender reassignment, marital or civil partner status, pregnancy or maternity, race, colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin, religion or belief and sexual orientation. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of the Company’s commitment to equal employment opportunity, we provide reasonable adjustments, to candidates during the recruitment process, including to individuals with disabilities. We want to create a safe space that welcomes everyone so please let us know how we can accommodate you. In case you have any accessibility requirements you can share that with our Talent Acquisition team prior to your interview stage, if applicable. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The legal bit</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By submitting your CV to ClearBank Limited you are providing your consent for us to use the information you provide for recruitment purposes. For more information on how we manage your data go and check out our Candidate Privacy Notice on the ClearBank website to see how we process, manage and look after your data. You are also allowing us to communicate with you by email and telephone for recruitment purposes. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/clearbank/associate-director-people-strategy-execution-london-153188","tags":["ClearBank Group Holdings"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London Office - 2/3 days a week","created_at":1791722406},{"slug":"av-solutions-engineer-388112","company_name":"Neweratech","title":"AV Solutions Engineer","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;Join New Era Technology, where People First is at the heart of everything we do. With a global team of over 3,000 professionals, we&#39;re committed to creating a workplace where everyone feels valued, empowered, and inspired to grow. Our mission is to securely connect people, places, and information with end-to-end technology solutions at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;At New Era, you&#39;ll join a team-oriented culture that prioritizes your personal and professional development. Work alongside industry-certified experts, access continuous training, and enjoy competitive benefits. Guided by our core attributes — putting people first, embracing continuous learning, and thriving through collaboration and inclusion — we nurture our people to deliver exceptional customer service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;If you want to make an impact in a supportive, growth-oriented environment, New Era is the place for you. Apply today and help us shape the future of work—together&lt;/p&gt;
