&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/zetaglobal/account-director-crm-london-307528","tags":["Client Management"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1791712511},{"slug":"reliability-engineer-derby-418217","company_name":"hellofresh","title":"Reliability Engineer","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title: &lt;/strong&gt;Reliability Engineer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Smart parc, Spondon, Derby DE21 7HW&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Monday to Friday, 40hrs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Let&#39;s Discuss What&#39;s On The Table For You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;● 70% off HelloFresh or Green Chef boxes&lt;br&gt;● Company pension scheme&lt;br&gt;● Gym membership&lt;br&gt;● Bupa private medical insurance (including dental &amp;amp; family cover options)&lt;br&gt;● Mental health first aiders and an employee assistance programme&lt;br&gt;● Nursery support scheme&lt;br&gt;● Cycle to work scheme&lt;br&gt;● Group Life Assurance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Play a key part in supporting our Employee Resource Groups: FreshVets, Black Heritage Network, NEU Network (Neurodiversity), GET (Gender Equality Team) and FreshPride&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Reliability Engineer you will be the site Subject Matter Expert (SME) within the team, for all controls systems, maintenance engineering, sensors, PLCs, communication protocols, and automation for the site. You will work with the facilities and maintenance teams and colleagues to maintain and repair conveyance, automation and facilities equipment to support operations uptime and improve reliability of our systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a hands-on manner to actively monitor, fault find and repair systems in order to provide a high level of equipment availability to internal customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform preventive maintenance and routine inspections on assigned automation, robotics and control panels.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform troubleshooting of assigned out of service equipment and correct issues, act as an escalation point for lower level technicians, and escalate to leadership and/or vendors as needed for additional troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document all work in the computerized maintenance management system (CMMS) and ticketing systems as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor all maintenance personnel in developing appropriate skill sets and knowledge of equipment specializing in automation, controls and robotics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead root cause analysis of major downtime events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a network resource for technical issues and lead network-wide root cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop maintenance personnel knowledge on intermediate to advanced automation, controls and robotics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering on commissioning of new controls systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit vendor work to provide feedback to leadership on quality of work and SLA performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and/or modify PMs to standardize across the network and increase effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified or Solid practical understanding in Mechatronics, Electrical &amp;amp; Electronic, Mechanical, or Manufacturing Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in Automation, Mechanical, or Maintenance Engineering, ideally within a manufacturing or production environment such as FMCG.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in PLC-controlled systems and automated processes, including programming, troubleshooting, repair, and maintenance of PLCs, HMIs, VFDs, and related control systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable interpreting technical manuals, engineering drawings, and schematics to support diagnostics and solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in both reactive and preventative maintenance, with a track record of handling second-line escalations and completing CMMS (Computerized Maintenance Management System) tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept in material handling systems, with exposure to flow analysis, capacity visualization, and process monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A confident communicator and mentor, capable of coaching junior engineers and stepping in as proxy for senior automation engineers when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in leading Root Cause Analysis, supporting CI (Continuous Improvement) initiatives, and familiar with DIQ and WMS systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be considered for this role, you’ll need to have the independent right to work in the UK, as we&#39;re unfortunately unable to provide sponsorship at this time.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next steps&lt;/strong&gt;: Your application will be reviewed and if successful, a member of the Talent Acquisition Team will be in touch within 2 weeks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are required to cooperate with HelloFresh in all health and safety matters. You are responsible for ensuring you take reasonable care of your own health, and safety as well as others who may be affected by the work activities you undertake. You must report incidents immediately and actively raise health and safety-related concerns to your Line Manager.&amp;nbsp;As part of our commitment to maintaining a safe and secure environment, we will process Disclosure and Barring Service (&lt;span class=&quot;il&quot;&gt;DBS&lt;/span&gt;) checks to the successful individual. Failure to disclose relevant information at application or throughout the process could affect your employment with the company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are currently a HelloFresh employee, please make sure you have discussed your application with your Line Manager.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/hellofresh/reliability-engineer-derby-418217","tags":["Supply Chain Management & Operations"],"job_types":[],"location":"Derby","created_at":1791712509},{"slug":"senior-project-manager-454094","company_name":"Ensono","title":"Senior Project Manager","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Ensono, our&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;purpose is to be a relentless ally, disrupting the status quo and unleashing our clients to Do Great Things!&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We enable our clients to achieve key business outcomes that reshape how our world runs. As an expert technology adviser and managed service provider with cross-platform certifications, Ensono empowers our clients to keep up with continuous change and embrace innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Developing impactful solutions is something we do together at Ensono because&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Ideas Start Here&lt;/strong&gt;. Great things happen when many voices are heard, and people are supported to run with their ideas. On our teams, you will be backed by leaders with a passion for our business. This is a place where your ideas can&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Do Great Things.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We can&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Do Great Things&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;because we have great Associates. The Ensono Core Values unify our diverse talents and are woven into how we do business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adventure starts here.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Here you will be a part of a team that encourages you to master your craft, ask tomorrow’s questions today, and chart your path. Our Associates focus on client impact with curiosity and a feeling of relentless commitment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role and what you will be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Project Manager provides senior-level expertise to plan, organise, control, and deliver large, complex infrastructure and data centre migration projects across Ensono&#39;s client portfolio. Operating within the Global Project and Implementation (GPI) practice, this role manages multiple company-wide initiatives simultaneously — from scope definition and budget planning through to delivery and post-implementation review. A key part of this position involves building and maintaining strong relationships with client sponsors and internal leaders, including regular on-site engagement at the client&#39;s London office. The Senior Project Manager interfaces directly with client executive management to understand critical business priorities and ensures every project is completed within agreed scope, quality, time, and cost constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Collaborate with stakeholders to ensure business requirements are clearly defined, understood, and documented&lt;br&gt;• Define project scope, risks, potential issues, and resource requirements at the outset of each engagement&lt;br&gt;• Ensure project benefits are realised while managing the impact of organisational change on the business and its clients&lt;br&gt;• Develop project phases and translate them into clear, measurable project plans&lt;br&gt;• Communicate internally and externally on delivery of work products, planning activities, and cross-organisational resource relationships&lt;br&gt;• Manage projects in full adherence to Ensono&#39;s project management methodology&lt;br&gt;• Manage project scope across mission, objectives, and requirements throughout the project lifecycle&lt;br&gt;• Manage project schedules, including key milestone dates and critical path tracking&lt;br&gt;• Lead the team in identifying project risks, issues, assumptions, and dependencies; act as the primary escalation point and drive effective mitigation strategies to maintain project goals&lt;br&gt;• Provide leadership and strategic direction to the project team across all phases of delivery&lt;br&gt;• Oversee all project work streams, including timeline adherence, quality of deliverables, risk management, issue escalation, and stakeholder collaboration&lt;br&gt;• Work with all stakeholders to ensure governance frameworks and continuous improvement or transformation plans are established and maintained&lt;br&gt;• Establish deadlines, assign tasks, and monitor and summarise project progress for all relevant parties&lt;br&gt;• Develop business insights through analysis of results and communicate key findings to management to support data-driven decision-making&lt;br&gt;• Secure appropriate resources and personnel in collaboration with management to ensure projects are delivered on time and within budget&lt;br&gt;• Escalate barriers, risks, and issues that may impact timelines or deliverables in a timely and appropriate manner&lt;br&gt;• Manage the development of polished executive-level presentations and deliver findings to internal associates and external clients clearly and concisely&lt;br&gt;• Manage project status reporting in line with prescribed timelines for each engagement&lt;br&gt;• Develop measurement processes and methods to assess progress towards project goals and outcomes&lt;br&gt;• Manage project costs and budgets throughout the full delivery lifecycle&lt;br&gt;• Facilitate cross-training to support job rotation and minimise gaps in assignment coverage&lt;br&gt;• Provide coaching and constructive feedback to all project team members&lt;br&gt;• Mentor less experienced associates within the project management practice&lt;br&gt;• Interface with client executive management on-site at the client&#39;s London office to understand and address critical business issues and concerns&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Proficient in MS Office and MS Project&lt;br&gt;• Strong financial management skills, including experience with project budgeting and cost control&lt;br&gt;• Effective team management skills with the ability to lead matrixed, cross-functional teams&lt;br&gt;• Strong leadership and strategic direction capabilities&lt;br&gt;• IT outsourcing knowledge&lt;br&gt;• Strong infrastructure management experience&lt;br&gt;• ITIL and/or ITSM knowledge&lt;br&gt;• Ability to organise and define work in complex or ambiguous situations&lt;br&gt;• Ability to travel to the client&#39;s office in London as required&lt;br&gt;• Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education and/or Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Management Information Systems (MIS), or equivalent experience&lt;br&gt;• Minimum of 7 years of complex IT programme and project management experience&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated experience managing large-scale infrastructure and data centre migration projects&lt;br&gt;• MBA or Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business, Computer Science, or Engineering preferred&lt;br&gt;• Project financial and revenue recognition experience preferred&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Benefits:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:440,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that great work deserves great rewards. In return for your ideas, commitment and ambition, we’ll give you a very competitive base salary and a range of benefits as soon as you join. On top of your highly competitive base salary, we offer:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly competitive salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prestigious sales and broader team recognition with Annual Presidents Club&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company equity incentive plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;27 days annual leave + plus bank holidays (increasing to 30 with length of service)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;½ day leave for your birthday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sabbatical options at 5-years &amp;amp; 10-years’ service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 days study leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 day charity leave to work for a charity of your choice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private healthcare for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced parental leaves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life and income protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payroll giving to your favorite charity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coaching &amp;amp; mentoring opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional perks such as discounted gym membership, cycle scheme, EAP and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this all sounds great, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/ensono/senior-project-manager-454094","tags":["E2373 PMaaS (MRR)"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1791712507},{"slug":"qa-engineer-london-196348","company_name":"Artificial Labs","title":"QA Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Artificial</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Help shape the future of specialty insurance</strong><br /><br />At Artificial, we’re building the next generation of technology for the specialty (re)insurance market. Our mission is to transform how brokers and carriers operate in complex markets by removing operational barriers and enabling smarter, faster decision-making.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use modern technology to solve real challenges for some of the world’s leading brokers and insurers. By automating the repetitive and structuring the complex, we help our partners unlock new opportunities for innovation and growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be joining a collaborative team that values curiosity, ownership, and continuous learning. We work in an environment where ideas are heard, support is built-in, and outcomes matter. Everyone here has the chance to make a tangible impact on our products, our customers, and the industry.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've just raised $45M (£33M) in Series B funding from lead investor CommerzVentures, new investor Move Capital, as well as all existing shareholders. This investment round gives us the room to grow with confidence, continue to innovate, and ensure that Artificial remains the first choice for brokers and carriers seeking a smarter way to trade digitally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us, and take the chance to be a part of something that will change the landscape of insurance for generations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a <strong>QA Engineer</strong> to join our growing Product QA function and take ownership of testing across Artificial's product portfolio and customer specifications. This role covers both manual testing execution and hands-on automation work, moving flexibly between Platform and Transform (customer configuration) work as needed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manual and automated testing execution:</strong> Own and execute both manual and automated test cases across Artificial's product suite and customer specifications - moving flexibly between Platform and Transform as priorities shift, and applying automation where it's the right fit and manual judgement where it isn't - including functional, regression, integration, and exploratory testing, ensuring thorough coverage before releases reach production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Test planning and design:</strong> Write clear, detailed test plans and test cases based on product requirements, acceptance criteria, and specification documents; identify edge cases and risk areas; ensure traceability between requirements and test coverage; maintain this as a growing knowledge base of product behaviour and testing approaches</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer specification testing:</strong> Test new and updated customer configurations and specifications to validate they meet requirements and behave correctly within the platform - reducing reliance on FDE for quality verification</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automation contribution:</strong> Write and maintain automated tests within our established framework and standards, applying your existing automation experience rather than starting from scratch; help transition high-value manual test cases into automated coverage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bug identification and reporting:</strong> Identify, document, and triage defects with clear reproduction steps, severity assessments, and supporting evidence in Linear; follow up with engineering teams to verify fixes and close the loop</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Regression testing:</strong> Execute regression test suites ahead of releases to catch unintended side effects; help maintain and expand the regression library as the product evolves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Quality within DDO+ modes:</strong> Support QA touch points across Discovery (smoke-testing prototypes and early builds), Delivery (thorough testing of bets and features during development cycles), and Optimisation (validating bug fixes and investigating production issues)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Work closely with Product Managers, Engineers, and Solutions/FDEs to understand requirements, clarify expected behaviour, and ensure alignment on quality expectations for each release or specification</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About You</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2-5 years of experience in a QA or software testing role, with a strong foundation in manual testing techniques</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solid hands-on experience with at least one test automation framework (e.g. Playwright, Cypress, or Selenium)</strong> - comfortable both executing manual tests and maintaining automated ones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to write clear, structured test plans and test cases from requirements and specifications</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with systematic testing approaches - functional, regression, integration, exploratory - and the judgement to know when each is appropriate</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent bug reporting skills - you write reproduction steps that engineers can act on immediately</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with defect tracking and test management tools (e.g. Linear, Jira, or equivalent)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A methodical, detail-oriented approach with strong analytical and problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working across multiple product areas and workstreams simultaneously </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private medical insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Income protection insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Life insurance of 4 * base salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">On-site gym and shower facilities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced maternity and paternity pay</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team social events and company parties</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Salary exchange on pension and nursery fees</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to Maji, the financial wellbeing platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company stock options managed through Ledgy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Milestone Birthday Bonus and a Life Events leave policy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous holiday allowance of 28 days plus national holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Home office and equipment allowance, and a company MacBook</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning allowance and leave to attend conferences or take exams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">YuLife employee benefits, including EAP and bereavement helplines</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For each new hire, we plant a tree through our partnership with Ecologi Action</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The best coffee machine in London, handmade in Italy and imported just for us!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re proud to be an equal opportunities employer and are committed to building a team that reflects the diverse communities around us. If there’s anything you need to make the hiring process more accessible, just let us know—we’re happy to make adjustments. You’re also welcome to share your preferred pronouns with us at any point.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Think you don’t meet every requirement? Please apply anyway. We value potential as much as experience, and we know that raw talent counts.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>As part of our hiring process, we’ll carry out some background checks. These may include a criminal record check, reviewing your credit history, speaking with previous employers and confirming your academic qualifications.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/artificial-labs/qa-engineer-london-196348","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1791711612},{"slug":"customer-success-engineer-london-108102","company_name":"incident.io","title":"Customer Success Engineer","description":"<h1>A little about us</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://incident.io">incident.io</a> is the AI software reliability platform trusted by engineering teams at Netflix, Etsy, and 2,000+ companies who can't afford downtime.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The stakes are real, the talent is insane, and somehow it's a genuinely lovely place to work. We all pull our weight, go the extra mile, and put in the bit of magic most companies don't have time for, all while having fun and never taking ourselves too seriously.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've raised $96 million from Index Ventures, Insight Partners, and Point Nine, and we're growing fast. There's never been a better time to join.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>The role in one line</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our first Customer Success Engineer in EMEA, you’ll help shape the team and make sure our most complex customers are built to scale, not just set up for go-live.</p><h1>What that looks like day to day</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Customer Success team is at the heart of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://incident.io">incident.io</a>. We understand customer challenges and deliver Incident Management solutions that make a real impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We take a customer-led approach, working closely with Product to understand and address each customer’s unique challenges. We go beyond satisfaction, aiming to delight customers at every stage and build long-term relationships based on trust, shared success, and mutual growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our first Customer Success Engineer in EMEA, this is a pivotal role with a real chance to shape the team as it grows. You’ll be a strategic technical partner in the post-sales lifecycle and a trusted advisor to our most complex customers, working with CSMs to own onboarding and expansion design. As leading organizations come to rely on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://incident.io">incident.io</a>, you’ll guide governance, scalable configuration, and long-term architecture so their incident management programs scale reliably across teams, not just at go-live. You’ll bridge Customer Success, Product, and Engineering, advocating for customers’ technical needs and influencing platform strategy within key accounts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Day to day, that means guiding complex migrations from legacy incident management platforms with operational continuity and clean foundations. It means owning onboarding and expansion design, advising on alerting strategy, escalation structures, workflow automation, and scalable configuration. You’ll act as a trusted advisor to engineering leaders, influencing platform design in complex environments, and establish durable architectural patterns and repeatable deployment frameworks that reduce misconfiguration and support burden. You’ll also partner with Product and Engineering to improve platform scalability and usability.</p><h1>Who you are</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re confident as a strategic technical partner in client-facing environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve architected complex SaaS implementations or led enterprise migrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think in systems and design solutions that scale across teams and regions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You explain complex technical concepts simply and steer customers toward pragmatic, maintainable solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have clear judgment on scope and ownership, knowing when to go deep and when to hand back to CSM or Support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can structure and drive technical onboarding and migration work-streams, partnering with CSMs to keep projects on track.</p></li></ul><h1>Supporting you</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work hard and we think life outside work matters just as much. Our benefits pack is built to support both.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Private medical insurance.</strong> Seriously good cover - we want you and the people you love to be looked after.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive annual leave.</strong> Showing up at your best requires switching off, and we make sure you have time to do that.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Friday of every month off.</strong> Yes, seriously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhanced pension.</strong> We put real money in, because future-you deserves better than an afterthought.</p></li><li><p style="min-