t<br />Location: London - Hybrid-Working: 3 days in office, 2 days from home</p><h2><br /><strong>ABOUT THE ROLE:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">APEXX is pioneering payment orchestration, transforming the global payments landscape with cutting-edge technology and innovation. As a leader in Fintech, we're committed to excellence, driving forward-thinking solutions that empower businesses worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Product Manager to own APEXX's Self-Service &amp; Onboarding domain. You will define and execute the product strategy that enables customers to onboard, configure, manage, and optimise their use of APEXX services independently, creating a scalable self-service experience that gives customers greater control and accelerates time-to-value.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a highly cross-functional role working across Product, Engineering, Design, Commercial, Customer Success, and Compliance to create scalable digital experiences that improve customer satisfaction and business efficiency.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own the end-to-end onboarding journey - from account creation and KYC/KYB orchestration to payment provider configuration, user management, and self-service administration - as part of a broader vision to give customers greater control over how they configure, manage, and optimise their use of the APEXX platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the vision, strategy, and roadmap for APEXX's self-service capabilities and Customer Portal, starting with the end-to-end merchant onboarding experience and progressively expanding customer control across the platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evolve the APEXX Customer Portal into a high-performing, intuitive, and flexible platform that enables customers to understand their payments through actionable data-driven insights and recommendations, and take meaningful actions directly within the platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and deliver scalable self-service capabilities spanning merchant onboarding, account and user administration, API credential management, payment provider configuration, routing rules, and wider platform configuration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive Product-Led Growth initiatives that increase adoption of APEXX capabilities, enable customers to expand their use of the platform, and unlock new commercial and market opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use customer research, product analytics, and experimentation to understand complex enterprise needs, identify opportunities, prioritise roadmap investments, and measure customer and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with Engineering, Design, Commercial, Customer Success, Compliance, and Operations to translate customer needs and product strategy into secure, scalable, performant, and intuitive experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities to leverage AI to simplify complex workflows, automate repetitive processes, surface actionable insights and recommendations, and provide intelligent in-product guidance.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>ABOUT YOU:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record in Product Management within SaaS, platform, fintech, or similarly complex digital products, with end-to-end ownership from discovery and strategy through delivery and measurable outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience owning and delivering sophisticated customer-facing portals, self-service capabilities, onboarding journeys, or platform configuration products, ideally within complex enterprise environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong product and systems thinking, with the ability to turn complex customer and operational workflows into intuitive, scalable, and reusable product capabilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of Product-Led Growth, with experience using product capabilities and customer experience to drive adoption, expansion, and commercial growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and data-driven approach, with experience using customer research, product analytics, and experimentation to inform decisions, prioritise effectively, and measure outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong product judgement and commercial awareness, with the ability to balance customer needs, business outcomes, technical constraints, and long-term platform scalability when making product decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to create clarity, influence decisions, and work effectively across Engineering, Design, Commercial, Customer Success, Compliance, and Operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in payments, fintech, or financial services would be highly advantageous.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>COMPENSATION &amp; BENEFITS:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Great people deserve great rewards. We believe in recognising the impact you make with competitive compensation and benefits that support you both at work and beyond.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Whether it's taking time to recharge, looking after your health, working from somewhere new, or investing in your growth, we've built a benefits package designed to help you thrive, because when our people do well, so does APEXX.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 <strong>Competitive Compensation: </strong>We offer competitive salaries that recognise your skills, experience, and the impact you make.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏖️ <strong>Generous Time Off:</strong> Take the time you need to rest and recharge with annual leave, public holidays, and wellbeing-focused time away from work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌍 <strong>Work From Anywhere:</strong> Enjoy the flexibility to work remotely from eligible locations for up to 90 days per year, subject to our Work From Anywhere policy.*</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">❤️ <strong>Comprehensive Health Insurance:</strong> Your wellbeing matters. We provide comprehensive health insurance which includes optical &amp; dental to help support you when it matters most.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🛡️ <strong>Life Insurance &amp; Critical Illness Protection: </strong>Additional protection for you and your loved ones when it’s needed most.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">👶 <strong>Enhanced Family Leave</strong>: Supporting you through life's biggest milestones with enhanced parental and family-friendly leave policies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📈 <strong>Learning &amp; Growth:</strong> We're invested in your development, with opportunities to learn, grow, and build a meaningful career at APEXX.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>WHO WE ARE &amp; WHERE WE ARE:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">APEXX is a global payment orchestration platform with teams across the UK &amp; India, helping enterprise businesses simplify the complexity of payments. For more than a decade, we've been building technology that enables merchants to connect to the world's payment ecosystem through a single, scalable integration.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our platform gives businesses access to <strong>200+ acquirers, 150+ alternative payment methods, and 10+ Buy Now, Pay Later providers</strong>, helping them optimise payment performance, improve acceptance rates, and expand into new markets with confidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Trusted by leading global brands including <strong>Ryanair, TUI, Hotelbeds, CarTrawler, Avon, and Jet2</strong>, we're redefining enterprise payments by making them smarter, faster, and more reliable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As we continue to grow, so do the opportunities to make an impact. Whether you're building products, solving complex engineering challenges, or supporting the teams behind them, you'll play a meaningful role in shaping the future of global payments at APEXX.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To learn more about APEXX and experience the dynamics of being part of our team, feel free to check out the provided media channels below:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>LinkedIn</strong>: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/apexxglobal/">https://www.linkedin.com/company/apexxglobal/</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Instagram</strong>: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/apexx.global/?hl=en">https://www.instagram.com/apexx.global/?hl=en</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Main</strong> <strong>Website</strong>: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://apexx.global/">https://apexx.global/</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">APEXX is an equal opportunities employer committed to encouraging equality, diversity, and inclusion among our employees and eliminating discrimination.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We do not accept speculative CVs or candidate profiles from Recruitment Agencies.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/apexx/senior-product-manager-self-service-onboarding-farringdon-10867","tags":["Product & Technology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London HQ","created_at":1791700804},{"slug":"executive-assistant-london-166116","company_name":"Outpost Technologies","title":"Executive Assistant","description":"<h2>🌍 About Outpost</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Global expansion is broken. Without a local entity, conversion rates fall, costs rise, and compliance gets messy. Outpost fixes it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Outpost is your modular back office for global commerce. Pick only what you need - tax, payments, treasury, or operations - and unlock new markets without the overhead. Sometimes we act as Merchant of Record, taking on tax and compliance risk. Other times, we give you the tools to do it yourself.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sell anything, anywhere. Without compromise.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🧠 The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring a second Executive Assistant to support our CEO.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We already have an EA, and she isn't going anywhere. You'll report to the CEO and work alongside her: she keeps inbound, customer routing and the investor-facing side, takes diary, travel, logistics, internal admin, and hiring coordination. You'll join to take a defined set of workstreams off that plate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Roughly 70% of this role is executive support. The other 30% is hiring - and that's where the leverage is. We run a five-stage interview loop across engineering, ops, product, GTM and tax, hiring around two people a month. Someone needs to own the machinery: scheduling across five calendars and four countries, keeping candidates warm, chasing feedback, making sure nobody good goes cold because a diary didn't line up.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a role for someone early in their career who is unusually organised and wants to learn how a company actually gets built. You won't be handed a finished process. You'll be shown how we do things today, and expected to make it better.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🧩 What You'll Do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the CEO's diary and logistics</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run scheduling day to day - booking, moving, protecting focus time, resolving clashes before they become problems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Book and manage international travel, and rebuild it when a flight moves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare meeting packs: who's in the room, what they want, what happened last time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track and chase the follow-ups nobody wrote down</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Do the work he never sees</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The highest-value work here is invisible. He shouldn't know it happened - he should just find the day went smoothly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fix problems before they reach him: the double-booking, the missing dial-in, the visa that needed renewing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do the quiet prep - background on a person he's meeting, what was agreed last time, the numbers checked before a deck goes out</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Anticipate. If a trip is booked, the transfer, the dinner and the buffer around the flight are already handled</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The fewer questions he has to ask you, the better you're doing the job</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own hiring coordination</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run scheduling across the full interview loop - five stages, multiple interviewers, several time zones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the pipeline clean: trackers, interview feedback, stage-by-stage conversion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build target lists for open roles and help manage outreach</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the candidate's point of contact - fast, warm, human. How we treat candidates is how we're judged</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate offers, references, contracts, start dates, and new-hire onboarding logistics</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep the company running</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support board and investor prep alongside the CEO, Chief of Staff and our senior EA</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help run internal comms: all-hands, offsites, company updates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage supplier, tooling and expense admin so nobody else has to think about it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spot the recurring problem and fix it permanently rather than solving it again next week</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>💥 Example Projects</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rebuild a full week of CEO travel in an afternoon after a fundraising meeting moves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take time-to-offer from three weeks to ten days by fixing scheduling and feedback bottlenecks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the candidate tracker that shows conversion at every interview stage, and run it weekly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the logistics for a board meeting: pre-reads, agenda, materials, follow-ups</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organise a company offsite for a team split across London, Amsterdam and beyond</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write down how you do your job so the next person can pick it up in a week</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🧱 What We're Looking For</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ideal background:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1–3 years in an EA, team assistant, recruiting coordinator or ops support role - ideally at a startup or fast-growing tech / fintech company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Any recruiting coordination exposure is a plus, but we'll teach it if you're quick</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable in a company without much process, because you've worked in one before</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent with modern tooling (Notion, Slack, Linear, ATS, scheduling tools and AI) and quick to pick up new ones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written English. You'll write on the CEO's behalf</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Signals we care about:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ridiculous bias for action - you solve, not observe</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extremely organised, and visibly so. Nothing gets dropped, nothing needs chasing twice</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong EQ - you know how to read a room, a candidate, or a blocker</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound judgement - you know what to decide yourself and what to escalate, and you sit on neither</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discreet. You'll see comp, term sheets and candidate conversations before most of the team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious and resourceful - you can figure anything out</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You improve what you touch. The second time you do something, it should be faster than the first</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What this role is not:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not a diary-only role - you'll own hiring, onboarding and internal operations too</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not a pure recruiter role - hiring is a third of the job, not the whole of it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not a role for someone who needs defined processes and hierarchy to be effective</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not a stepping stone you can coast through. The exposure is real, and so is the pace</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🚀 Why This Role Is Different</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most assistant roles are about keeping someone else's life tidy. This one is about making a company move faster.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own hiring coordination, which at our stage is one of the highest-leverage things we do — the people you help bring in will shape what Outpost becomes. And you'll get a front-row view of a Series A fintech being built, with two people above you invested in teaching you how it works.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We expect whoever is in this role to grow rapidly, and we'll back you every step of the way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🦾 Outpost Team</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our team were leaders at Revolut, Airwallex, Adyen, Sumup and Wayflyer - and we're backed by top-tier investors who have built or backed some of the world's leading fintechs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🧾 What We Offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity and salary in a well-funded startup</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to own your work and move fast</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">World-class training from operators who've scaled globally</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A global mission with real impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Low politics, high output</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Chance to grow into a senior role fast</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A culture of builders, not talkers</p></li></ul><h2>🌎 Reach Out</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learn more</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/Outpost-Culture-18aa047bb9af800b8f6ff5f5c83174b1?pvs=21"><u>Outpost Culture</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.littlegoatlabs.com/"><u>Outpost founder</u></a></p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/outpost-technologies/executive-assistant-london-166116","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1791700804},{"slug":"senior-support-specialist-uk-london-186280","company_name":"Ema","title":"Senior Support Specialist- UK","description":"<h1><strong>About Ema</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ema builds AI Employees for HR, IT and Finance. Our AI Employees take on the busy work across the employee experience, from recruiting, onboarding and benefits to IT support, invoice processing and payroll, so people can spend their time on work that needs them. Founded by former executives from Google, Coinbase, Flipkart, and Okta, our team includes engineers from premier tech companies and graduates of Stanford, MIT, UC Berkeley, CMU, and IITs.<br /><br />We are backed by industry leading investors including Accel, Naspers/Prosus, Creaegis, Section32, and angels like Sheryl Sandberg and Dustin Moskovitz. Headquartered in Silicon Valley and with offices in London, Bangalore and Vancouver, Ema is at the frontier of what Agentic AI can do in production. We ship real systems that run real business processes at scale.</p><h1><strong>Role: Senior Support Specialist (Enterprise Agentic AI)</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Company:</strong> Ema Unlimited Inc.<br /> <strong>Location:</strong> London<br /> <strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full-time/Remote</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>1. About Ema (Why Ema)</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ema is building the world’s first <strong>Universal AI Employee</strong> — a production-grade agentic AI platform that automates real enterprise workflows across HR, IT, Finance, and Operations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ema’s customers do not run demos. They replace <strong>mission-critical, manual business processes</strong> with agentic AI systems that operate across multiple SaaS tools, APIs, and human-in-the-loop workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this world, <strong>support is not reactive</strong>.  Support is <strong>production reliability, trust preservation, and system learning</strong>.  At Ema, Senior Technical Support Specialists are <strong>operators of live AI systems</strong>, not ticket handlers.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>2. Role Overview</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The <strong>Senior Support Engineer</strong> owns the <strong>health, reliability, and trustworthiness</strong> of Ema’s deployed agentic AI systems in production.  This role sits at the intersection of:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI behavior</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Workflow orchestration</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enterprise integrations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer trust</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineering feedback loops</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is:  ❌ Not L1 / call-center support,  ❌ Not a “just escalate to engineering” role, ❌ Not reactive firefighting only</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This <strong>is</strong>: A senior technical escalation role, A production debugging and RCA role, A partner to Engineering, Product, and Implementation, A role with real authority during incidents</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>3. Impact of the Role</strong></h2><h3><strong>Impact at Ema</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are the <strong>last line of defense</strong> between a production issue and customer trust erosion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prevent small failures from turning into account-level crises</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You ensure learnings from incidents improve the product and delivery systemically<br /></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Impact on Customers</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customers trust Ema because <strong>issues are handled competently and transparently</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI failures are explained, mitigated, and prevented — not hand-waved</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Production stability improves over time, not degrades</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Impact on Your Career</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You gain rare experience operating <strong>agentic AI systems in production</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You build deep expertise across AI, integrations, and workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can grow into <strong>Reliability Engineering, Implementation Leadership, or Product-facing roles</strong></p></li></ul><h2><strong>4. Core Problems You Will Solve</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diagnosing failures in <strong>multi-agent AI workflows</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deeply understanding Ema’s platform and providing workarounds/alternate approaches to customers facing issues<strong><br /></strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debugging issues spanning:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI behavior (false positives / negatives)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Workflow logic</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrations (HRIS, ITSM, IAM, Finance)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Platform configuration<br /></p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handling Sev-1 / Sev-2 customer specific incidents calmly under customer pressure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help Engineering &amp; Product teams Prevent repeated incidents through disciplined RCA</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Converting noisy customer complaints into <strong>high-signal engineering feedback</strong></p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>5. Jobs To Be Done</strong></h2><h3><strong>5.1 Production Issue Ownership</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own customer-reported issues from intake to resolution adhering strictly to SLAs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take responsibility for diagnosis, coordination, and closure; Importantly, provide workarounds to customers to unblock them while engineering fix is made</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure no issue is “lost” between teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as technical owner even when multiple teams are involved</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h3><strong>5.2 Debugging, Diagnosis &amp; Sev 1/2 Issue Resolution</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debug agentic workflows end-to-end</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Trace failures across agents, tools, integrations, and humans-in-the-loop</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify whether issues are caused by:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Model behavior</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prompt / policy logic</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Workflow orchestration</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integration constraints</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer configuration<br /></p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide clear, actionable root cause summaries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Resolve Sev 1 / Sev 2 Client issues; Escalate to the right team to help solve and close the issue. Keep customer communication calm, factual, and confidence-building</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h3><strong>5.4 Customer Communication &amp; Trust</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate during incidents without speculation or panic</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explain AI failures in a way customers can understand</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set realistic recovery timelines</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rebuild trust post-incident through transparency and follow-through<br /></p></li></ul><h3><strong>5.6 Feedback Loops to Engineering &amp; Product</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write high-signal bug reports and incident summaries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advocate for fixes based on <strong>customer impact</strong>, not noise</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help Product understand real production behavior</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure support insights influence roadmap and quality improvement</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h3><strong>5.7 Support Operations &amp; Excellence</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve runbooks, playbooks, and diagnostics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve on-call hygiene and escalation clarity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentor junior support engineers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Raise the overall support bar at Ema</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>6. Traits We’re Looking For</strong></h2><h3><strong>Technical &amp; Diagnostic Strength</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent debugging instincts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable operating in ambiguous systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to isolate root cause across layers</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Ownership &amp; Reliability Mindset</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Issues do not bounce — they get owned</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Calm during incidents</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bias toward permanent fixes<br /></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Judgment &amp; Communication</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knows when to escalate and when not to</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can say “we don’t know yet” credibly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicates clearly with both engineers and customers<br /></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Cultural Fit</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Low ego, high accountability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Truth-seeking over blame</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Respects both customer urgency and engineering quality</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>7. Required Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>6–9+ years</strong> in senior technical support, reliability, or production engineering roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting <strong>enterprise SaaS platforms in production</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">APIs and integrations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Distributed systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Logs, traces, and diagnostics</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience handling escalations and incidents</p></li><li><p style="min-heigh