ting sustainable, multi-year sourcing channels for high-potential candidates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build inclusive and equitable intern programs</strong> with structured learning objectives, meaningful core projects, and mentor/buddy pairing systems for every cohort</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive global campus recruitment</strong>: represent Mistral at career fairs, host on-campus events, and develop targeted employer branding strategies for student markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build scalable systems and best practices</strong> — workflows, documentation, and tools — to support rapid growth across geographies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Embody our culture</strong> as an ambassador for Mistral, on campus and internally.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proven experience:</strong> 5+ years in recruiting, preferably in tech, high-growth, or competitive environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Early careers depth:</strong> Exposure to global early careers, internships, or graduate recruitment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partnership expertise:</strong> Expertise in international school and university partnership development and global campus recruitment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Program building:</strong> Demonstrated experience building inclusive and equitable intern programs, with excellent project management skills and exceptional attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data-driven mindset:</strong> Skilled at analyzing metrics to solve problems and optimize recruitment processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global perspective:</strong> Experience with international hiring and fluent English communication; French is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-