ro","title":"DevOps Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Swarm Aero is redefining air power, building the largest swarming UAV and the most versatile swarming aircraft network in the world. The company is moving quickly to launch the first aircraft designed specifically for swarming, as well as the Command &amp; Control software to mobilize swarms of thousands of heterogeneous autonomous assets and empower human operators to achieve superhuman results.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team has created and exited multiple startups, negotiated defense deals worth billions of dollars, and designed and built 30+ novel aircraft, with aerospace experience from Scaled Composites, Airbus, Archer Aviation, Blue Origin, and Boom Supersonic.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Swarm Aero</strong><br /> Swarm Aero builds Group 5 autonomous aircraft and Legion, our command and control platform for coordinating UAV swarms. We're backed by Founders Fund, Khosla Ventures, and Coatue, and our software is already running on real programs and real hardware. Legion is the layer operators actually touch, and it needs to ship fast, run reliably, and deploy anywhere our customers need it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong><br /> You'll be a core member of the team that builds and runs the infrastructure behind Legion. Working alongside our DevSecOps lead, you'll own day-to-day pipelines, environments, and deployments so our engineers can move quickly without breaking the things operators depend on. This is a hands-on role for someone who likes building systems more than writing tickets about them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain CI/CD pipelines that take Legion from commit to production across multiple environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage infrastructure as code for cloud and on-prem deployments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run and scale containerized services on Kubernetes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build out observability: monitoring, logging, alerting, and on-call tooling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Package and deploy Legion to customer environments, including travel to customer and test sites when deployments require it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with our DevSecOps lead to bake security and compliance requirements into the platform from the start</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help engineers across Legion ship faster by improving developer tooling and environments</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4 to 8 years in DevOps, platform, SRE, or infrastructure engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong hands-on experience with Kubernetes, containers, and infrastructure as code (Terraform or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and owning CI/CD pipelines in a production environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid Linux and networking fundamentals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scripting in Python, Go, or Bash</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Active Secret clearance or higher strongly preferred; must be able to obtain and maintain a US security clearance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel to customer and test sites</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience deploying to air-gapped, disconnected, or edge environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in defense tech, government programs, or regulated environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting real-time or mission-critical systems</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ITAR requirement</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a U.S. citizen, lawful permanent resident of the U.S., protected individual as defined by 8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3), or eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Swarm Aero is an equal opportunity employer. We value diverse backgrounds and experiences and make employment decisions without regard to race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, or disability.<br /><br /><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meaningful equity in a high-growth defense technology company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive base salary commensurate with experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Medical, dental, vision, and 401k</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PTO and paid sick leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monthly wellness stipend</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Daily catered lunch (office)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct impact on a critical national security mission</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A world-class team of engineers and operators solving genuinely hard problems</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: $140K – $185K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • $140K – $185K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/swarmaero/remote-devops-engineer-28165","tags":["Legion"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1791628805},{"slug":"lead-talent-acquisition-emea-paris-210555","company_name":"Pelico","title":"Lead Talent Acquisition EMEA","description":"<h2><strong>About Pelico</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Traditional industrial manufacturing systems were built for predictability. Supply chains no longer are. Today, real-time data is buried in legacy tools that weren't designed for constant disruption. By the time an issue surfaces, it has already snowballed, sending everyone into firefighting mode. Pelico exists to close the gap between production plans and the daily reality on the factory floor.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've built the manufacturing orchestration platform trusted by the world's most complex industrial operations : companies like Airbus, Boeing, Safran, Eaton, and Cartier. Our AI connects fragmented supply chain, production, and quality data into a single live operational picture — then puts AI agents to work anticipating disruptions, simulating recovery options, and keeping every team aligned before small problems become expensive ones.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2019 and backed by General Catalyst, 83North, and Serena, we've raised $72M and are growing fast — 300% year-over-year revenue growth, deployed in 15+ countries, and supporting factories worldwide. We're headquartered in Paris, with offices in Miami, London and Amsterdam, and we're just getting started.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a rare chance to join a company that's redefining an industry that hasn't been disrupted in decades — from the inside.</p><h2>What You’ll Do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape the talent strategy for EMEA</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build our EMEA recruiting strategy from the ground up: the processes, playbooks, and operating rhythm that let us scale hiring with quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Raise talent quality and density: define what great looks like for each role, coach hiring managers on how to spot and hire the right people, and track quality of hire.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with People leadership on a data-driven talent strategy, using funnel metrics and market insights to forecast needs and influence hiring decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create our EMEA employer brand strategy, from job sites and career page to school partnerships and events, with a great candidate experience at every step.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stay hands-on: recruit every day</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own full-cycle recruiting from kickoff through offer acceptance, with a focus on tech roles and support on select business hires.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run creative, outbound-first sourcing and build talent pipelines before needs become urgent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise hiring managers on candidate profiles, interview design, and calibration.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build a TA function powered by AI</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embed AI across sourcing, market research, candidate engagement, and recruiting operations, and keep testing new ways of working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up the tools and ATS (Ashby) that let the team scale.</p></li></ul><h2>About You</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-powered and innovative</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You design recruiting processes where AI does the heavy lifting, and you know when to automate and when to keep the human touch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re resourceful and curious, and you bring ideas to the team rather than waiting to be asked.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>6+ years of tech recruiting experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a proven track record hiring tech profiles (engineering, data, product) through full-cycle recruiting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable as a generalist, hiring across functions and seniority levels as needs evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re skilled at outbound sourcing and experienced with modern ATS platforms.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale-up and agile mindset</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve worked in a high-growth, fast-changing environment and love building from zero.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think like an owner, balancing speed with quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You influence leaders with sound judgment and a genuine care for candidate experience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">International recruiting experience across multiple markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing or mentoring recruiters.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why Pelico</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building something genuinely hard and genuinely important. Here's what that comes with:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meaningful equity - you're building this with us, so you'll own a piece of it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary benchmarked to your market</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible, hybrid work model - we care about output, not face time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health, dental, and vision coverage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning &amp; development budget - we invest in people who invest in themselves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunity to work with some of the world's most complex and fascinating manufacturing operations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A team that takes the work seriously without taking themselves too seriously</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Pelico is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to building a diverse team and an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/pelico/lead-talent-acquisition-emea-paris-210555","tags":["Internal Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1791618014},{"slug":"engineering-internships-2027-paris-414780","company_name":"Nabla","title":"Engineering Internships 2027","description":"<h2><strong>About Nabla</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a team of entrepreneurs, clinicians and engineers committed to bringing back joy to the practice of medicine.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Together with a community of clinician innovators, we’ve harnessed the best of machine learning science to develop Nabla: the leading AI assistant that’s restoring the human connection at the heart of healthcare. By streamlining clinical documentation, Nabla is helping clinicians focus on what matters most - patient care. Today, over 100,000+ clinicians across 130+ healthcare organizations trust Nabla to support how they deliver care every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re at the start of an ambitious journey: Ambient listening, dictation, coding, and command capabilities are all converging into a proactive assistant that intuitively streamlines clinical and financial workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by a recent $70M Series C, we’re hiring to build the next generation of clinical AI and improve the lives of clinicians and patients everywhere.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a great time to join us!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Early Careers: Software Engineering &amp; Machine Learning </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for <strong>early-career engineers</strong> who want to learn fast, work with experienced mentors, and make a real impact from day one. You’ll join a collaborative, mission-driven team where technical curiosity and humility matter as much as skill.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Paris (Hybrid)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start Date:</strong> 2027 (or as early as possible)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commitment:</strong>  Internship-to-hire</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we Offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real Impact from Day One:</strong> You won’t be stuck with small tasks: you’ll contribute to real features and products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning Everywhere:</strong> We believe in mentorship, pair programming, and leveling up together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lean, Ambitious Team:</strong> Be part of a fast-moving, deeply technical culture where your contributions matter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Healthcare Mission:</strong> Help doctors, nurses, and care teams spend more time with Patients</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Career Launchpad:</strong> Many interns convert to full-time, and early engineers grow quickly.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We work across multiple domains:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Apps:</strong> Web app, frontend logic, UI/UX</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Platform:</strong> Backend services, infrastructure, APIs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Core (ML):</strong> Algorithms, models, data systems</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your DNA</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Currently pursuing or recently graduated in <strong>Computer Science, Engineering, Applied Math, or a related field</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable coding in at least one: <strong>Java, Kotlin, Python, or TypeScript</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passionate about AI, data, or building meaningful product features.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious, collaborative, and excited to learn.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Humble and resilient — you ask questions, take feedback, and grow.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice-to-Haves (but not required)</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Internship or personal projects in AI, full-stack, or backend systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with React, GraphQL, or cloud infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of CI/CD, Docker, or automated testing.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’ll see us on campus at:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Télécom Paris</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Forum Trium</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ENSIMAG</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CentraleSupélec</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">École Polytechnique</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">EPFL</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Forum Organisation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meet us there and tell us what excites you.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Life at Nabla</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">When you become a part of our company, you join a team of excellence-driven, curious, and genuinely kind individuals. Together, we're committed to making clinicians' lives easier and improving healthcare experiences for everyone. We believe in a world where clinicians can focus on what they were trained to do - caring for their patients, and where no patient feels their visit was rushed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We come to work excited to leverage AI to do more for clinicians. We’re obsessed with our users’ satisfaction and we actively seek out opportunities to engage one-on-one with clinicians to understand how Nabla can better help. We consistently look for ways to improve and do not shy away from doing the work to excel. Whether it’s a feature our users asked for, or a new article for our blog, we prioritize collaboration to deliver exceptional outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We love having fun as much as we love work. Our #nablabla channel is as active as our #feature-show-off channel, we exercise during the work day at least 3 times a week (yoga, running, pilates, or HIIT, your choice!), enjoy regular off-sites to gather the team, and travel to see each other in places like NY, Paris, San Francisco, and many other vibrant cities. Oh, and we’re constantly snacking on chocolate or nuts!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this sounds like an environment you’ll thrive in, we look forward to reading your application!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our Values at Nabla</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining Nabla means being part of a team that shares a commitment to excellence, humility, growth, and inclusion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Every day is a new chance to excel</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We aim for nothing less than the best and are willing to put in the effort and dedication required to exceed standards. We learn from yesterday’s failures and do better every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stay humble</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">There’s no place for ego in our team. Our collective success is more important than individual achievements. We see humility as wisdom — keeping focus on the bigger picture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Feedback is a gift</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We embrace feedback and foster a culture of trust and respect that helps everyone grow. We communicate openly about both achievements and challenges, and we actively involve each other in finding solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Committed to diversity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We recognize the ongoing challenge of diversity in tech. Our responsibility starts with fostering an inclusive environment where everyone feels empowered to be their authentic selves and do their best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Diversity &amp; Inclusion</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diversity and inclusivity are fundamental values at Nabla. We embrace individuals from various backgrounds, including race, gender, educational history, sexual orientation, and beyond.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an equal opportunity employer, we actively seek out and welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds, believing that a wide range of perspectives enriches our team and enhances our ability to innovate and thrive.</p><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Avoid recruitment scams: Stay safe and informed</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">There is an active employment scam which is now using Nabla to collect personal information or financial scams. If you’re contacted by a Nabla recruiter, please ensure whomever is contacting you truly represents Nabla and is utilizing a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://nabla.com">nabla.com</a> email address. We will never ask for the exchange of any money or credit card details during the recruitment process. Nabla utilizes a hiring platform for all applications; please be aware of any suspicious email activity from people who could be pretending to be recruiters or senior professionals at Nabla. You can find more information following this <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://consumer.ftc.gov/consumer-alerts/2023/05/scammers-are-hijacking-job-ads-heres-how-spot-fakes">link</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>Nabla does not accept unsolicited CVs from recruiters or employment agencies in response to the Nabla Careers page or a Nabla social media post. Any unsolicited CVs, including those submitted directly to hiring managers, are deemed to be the property of Nabla.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/nabla/engineering-internships-2027-paris-414780","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris office","created_at":1791618010},{"slug":"field-sales-team-lead-lyon-french-and-english-speaking-136479","company_name":"Lightspeedhq","title":"Field Sales Team Lead, Lyon (French and English Speaking)","description":"<h2>Hi there! Thanks for stopping by 👋</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you actively looking for a new opportunity? Or just checking the market? Well… you<br />might just be in the right place!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a <strong>Team Lead, Field Sales </strong>to join our growing EMEA team in Lyon. This is an opportunity to build on the foundations of our Lyon sales team. Working closely with the Senior Manager, Outbound, you’ll coach and support the team, continue shaping our ways of working and play an important role in growing our presence in the market. You’ll join a team with ambitious growth plans and have high visibility across the organisation, with the opportunity to make a meaningful impact as the team expands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll be doing:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the Senior Manager, Outbound, to mentor, motivate and develop the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide regular coaching, training and feedback to help team members grow their sales careers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help the team consistently achieve monthly, quarterly and annual targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyse pipeline and performance metrics, identify opportunities and turn insights into action.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support outbound initiatives that improve team performance and market reach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Partnerships, Inbound, Implementation and Marketing to strengthen our customer journey and ways of working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help grow the Lyon team’s culture, operating rhythm and local market presence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to hiring and onboarding new team members as the team grows.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you bring to the team:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a candidate who has experience with the following:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience coaching or leading a sales team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">B2B sales experience, ideally in technology, solution sales or fintech.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong understanding of sales best practices and a proven ability to close.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of meeting or exceeding sales targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A data-driven approach to decision-making and a genuine interest in performance metrics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A passion for coaching and helping others develop.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to thrive in a competitive, dynamic and target-driven environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An entrepreneurial mindset, with a bias toward action and the flexibility to adapt as priorities evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ownership and energy to help build something new in a launch-phase environment</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Even better if you have (but not necessary):</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in the hospitality industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with POS systems</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><h2><strong>What’s in it for you?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Come live the Lightspeed experience...</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to do your job in a truly flexible environment;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlock your potential with our growth program, paving the way for promotions and career advancement;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine career opportunities in a company that’s creating new jobs every day;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in a team big enough for growth but lean enough to make a real impact.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>… and enjoy a range of benefits that’ll keep you happy, healthy and (not) hungry:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed share scheme (we are all owners)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health &amp; Wellness Credit- expense up to 400 EUR per year towards your gym membership, yoga classes, a new bike or whatever else you do for your health</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental Health Support through the Modern Health App- whether it is meditation, coaching or counseling you need - each employee gets access to this platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time off to volunteer and give back to your community</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transit benefit if you travel by public transport to the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch reimbursement on the days you work from our Paris office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health insurance with attractive guarantee plan</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To all recruitment agencies: Lightspeed does not accept unsolicited agency resumes. If we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy, Lightspeed will not be responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Lightspeed is a proud equal opportunity employer and we are committed to creating an inclusive and barrier-free workplace. Lightspeed welcomes and encourages applications from people with disabilities. Accommodations are available on request for candidates taking part in all aspects of the selection process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Where to from here?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Obviously, this has to be mutually beneficial: we want you to step into a role you love, and we want to offer you a place you’re proud to come to every day. For a glimpse into our world check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/careers/">career page here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed is building communities through commerce, and we need people from all backgrounds and lived experiences to do that. We were founded in 2005, in Montreal’s gay village and our original members were all part of the LGBTQ+ community. The ethos of our business has been about inclusion from the very beginning, and we strive to provide a workplace where everyone belongs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who we are:</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Powering the businesses that are the backbone of the global economy, Lightspeed's one-stop commerce platform helps merchants innovate to simplify, scale, and provide exceptional customer experiences. Our cloud commerce solution transforms and unifies online and physical operations, multichannel sales, expansion to new locations, global payments, financial solutions, and connection to supplier networks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Montréal, Canada in 2005, Lightspeed is dual-listed on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: LSPD) and Toronto Stock Exchange (TSX: LSPD). With teams across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific, the company serves retail, hospitality, and golf businesses in over 100 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed handles your information in accordance with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="c-link" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/legal/applicant-privacy-statement/">Applicant Privacy Statement</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/lightspeedhq/field-sales-team-lead-lyon-french-and-english-speaking-136479","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lyon","created_at":1791618009},{"slug":"head-of-formal-verification-hybrid-219488","company_name":"Lubis Eda","title":"Head of Formal Verification (m/f/d)","description":"<br><strong>Your mission</strong><p><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">You own the direction of our formal verification business. Our managers keep delivery predictable. You decide what the organisation becomes.<br><br>You report to the CEO and are a member of the executive leadership team. You carry the FV consulting business as a whole — where it goes, how it performs, who leads it — and you answer for it. You will not solve verification problems, and you will rarely run a project or an account yourself. Concretely, you own:<br><br></span><ul><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;"><strong>Direction</strong>. The roadmap for FV consulting