eal tasks at the crossroads of legal thinking, AI prompting, <strong>and making the commercial case to a customer</strong>.</li><li>Meet the team in our Zurich office.</li><li>Mutual decision, and we welcome you on board.</li></ol></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/legartis/legal-ai-counsel-zurich-495551","tags":["Legal AI Counsel","Legal Tech","Legal Engineering","AI","Zurich"],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1791673781},{"slug":"senior-financial-accountant-80-100-rotkreuz-196122","company_name":"enovetic ag","title":"Senior Financial Accountant (80-100%)","description":"<br><strong>Über uns</strong><p>enovetic entwickelt und betreibt eine führende Plattform, die Arbeit, Gesundheit und Vermögen intelligent verbindet. Damit vereinfachen wir die Administration dieser Bereiche und gestalten zentrale Interaktionen zwischen Menschen, Arbeitgebern und Anbietern digital, effizient und medienbruchfrei.<br><br>Du möchtest anspruchsvolle Finanzthemen mitgestalten und deine Erfahrung in einer modernen, zukunftsorientierten Finanzorganisation einbringen? Für unser unternehmensinternes Accounting, Controlling und Reporting innerhalb der Division Finance, Risk &amp; Compliance suchen wir dich als Senior Financial Accountant. Dabei bist du Teil eines kleinen, engagierten Teams und arbeitest eng mit deinen Kolleginnen und Kollegen zusammen.<br><br>In dieser vielseitigen Schlüsselrolle stellst du eine korrekte, effiziente und termingerechte Finanzbuchhaltung unserer Gruppengesellschaften sowie ein verlässliches Reporting sicher. Du verantwortest das operative Tagesgeschäft und die Abschlussprozesse, wirkst bei Konsolidierung, Konzernrechnung und Budgetierung mit und entwickelst unsere Finanzorganisation mit digitalen Lösungen, automatisierten Prozessen und aussagekräftigen Reporting-Strukturen aktiv weiter.</p><br><strong>Was dich erwartet</strong><p><ul><li>Du steuerst das operative Tagesgeschäft und sorgst für eine korrekte Buchhaltung unserer Schweizer Gruppengesellschaften – inklusive KTG und Rendement.</li><li>Du erstellst Monats-, Quartals- und Jahresabschlüsse sowie MWST-Abrechnungen abschlusssicher, zuverlässig und termingerecht.</li><li>Du wirkst bei Budgetierung, Konzernkonsolidierung und Konzernrechnung mit.</li><li>Du entwickelst aussagekräftige Finanz- und Managementreports mit MS Power BI.</li><li>Du treibst die Digitalisierung und Automatisierung unserer Finanzprozesse voran und gestaltest moderne Tools und Systeme aktiv mit.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Was du mitbringst</strong><p><ul><li>Du verfügst über einen eidg. Fachausweis im Finanz- und Rechnungswesen oder eine gleichwertige höhere Weiterbildung in Finance, Accounting oder Controlling.</li><li>Du bringst mehrjährige Erfahrung im Finanz- und Rechnungswesen sowie fundierte Praxis in Monats-, Quartals- und Jahresabschlüssen mit.</li><li>Du begeisterst dich für die Digitalisierung und Automatisierung von Finanzprozessen und möchtest Systeme, Datenqualität und Reporting-Strukturen aktiv weiterentwickeln.</li><li>Du gehst sicher mit Excel um und verfügst idealerweise über Erfahrung mit MS Power BI sowie in Konzernrechnung und Konsolidierung.</li><li>Du arbeitest analytisch, strukturiert und lösungsorientiert, packst gerne selbst mit an und kommunizierst sicher auf Deutsch und Englisch.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Was wir bieten</strong><p><ul><li>Du arbeitest an einem modernen Standort in Rotkreuz mit zeitgemässer Infrastruktur und sehr guter Erreichbarkeit.</li><li>Du gestaltest deinen Arbeitsalltag flexibel – mit hybriden Arbeitsmöglichkeiten und Arbeitszeiten, die Beruf und Privatleben gut vereinbaren lassen.</li><li>Du profitierst von attraktiven Anstellungsbedingungen inklusive überdurchschnittlicher Pensionskassenlösung.</li><li>Du erhältst Unterstützung für deinen Arbeitsweg, unter anderem durch Beiträge an öV- und Park+Rail-Abonnemente sowie firmeneigene Parkplätze.</li><li>Du nutzt bei Bedarf Ladestationen vor Ort und ein Inhouse-Gym für Bewegung und Ausgleich im Arbeitsalltag.</li></ul><br>Klingt das nach deinem nächsten Schritt? Dann freuen wir uns auf deine Bewerbung. Weitere Informationen über unsere Produkte und unser Unternehmen findest du hier: <br><a href="//www.enovetic.ch">www.enovetic.ch</a><br><br><br></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/enovetic-ag/senior-financial-accountant-80-100-rotkreuz-196122","tags":["Buchhaltung","Controlling","Abschlüsse","MWST","Konzernkonsolidierung","Konzernrechnung","Budget","Digitalisierung"],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"Rotkreuz","created_at":1791673766},{"slug":"remote-value-strategist-187622","company_name":"ElevenLabs","title":"Value Strategist","description":"<h2>About ElevenLabs</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenLabs is an AI research and product company transforming how we interact with technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched in January 2023 with the first human-like AI voice model. Today, we serve millions of users and thousands of businesses - from fast-growing startups to large enterprises like Deutsche Telekom and Meta. Our investors are some of the world's most prominent, including Andreessen Horowitz, ICONIQ Growth and Sequoia. We've raised $781M in funding and our last valuation was $22B - multiples of 11, always.<br /><br />We have expanded from voice into three main platforms:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAgents enables businesses to deliver seamless and intelligent customer experiences, with the integrations, testing, monitoring, and reliability necessary to deploy voice and chat agents at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenCreative empowers creators and marketers to generate and edit speech, music, image, and video across 70+ languages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAPI gives developers access to our leading AI audio foundational models.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everything we do is the result of the creativity and commitment of our team - builders doing the best work of their lives. We are researchers, engineers, and operators. IOI medalists and ex-founders. If you want to work hard and create lasting positive impact, we want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we work</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-velocity: </strong>Rapid experimentation, lean autonomous teams, and minimal bureaucracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact not job titles: </strong>We don’t have job titles. Instead, it’s about the impact you have. No task is above or beneath you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI first:</strong> We use AI to move faster with higher-quality results. We do this across the whole company—from engineering to growth to operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellence everywhere: </strong>Everything we do should match the quality of our AI models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global team: </strong>We prioritize your talent, not your location.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Innovative culture:</strong> You’ll be part of a generational opportunity to define the trajectory of AI, surrounded by a team pushing the boundaries of what’s possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth paths: </strong>Joining ElevenLabs means joining a dynamic team with countless opportunities to drive impact - beyond your immediate role and responsibilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; development</strong>: ElevenLabs proactively supports professional development through an annual discretionary stipend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Social travel</strong>: We also provide an annual discretionary stipend to meet up with colleagues each year, however you choose.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Annual company offsite: </strong>Each year, we bring the entire team together in a new location - past offsites have included Croatia and Italy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Co-working</strong>: If you’re not located near one of our main hubs, we offer a monthly co-working stipend.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenLabs is looking for a Value Strategist to help our customers identify, quantify, and realize the business value of ElevenLabs across our portfolio, with a primary focus on ElevenAgents.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior individual contributor role within our global Revenue organization, spanning the full customer lifecycle from early sales conversations through proof of concept, deployment, renewal, and expansion. You will work directly with customers and prospects to understand their businesses, build the case for investment, and establish how that value will be measured over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">On our most strategic accounts, Deployment Strategists in our Forward Deployed Engineering team already build account-specific business cases and ROI narratives as part of delivery. You will partner with them rather than duplicate that work. Your mandate is the value discipline across the whole book: the Enterprise, Mid-Market, and Commercial accounts where no one is embedded, and where value today is quantified deal by deal or not at all. You will build the frameworks, benchmarks, calculators, and playbooks that let every seller articulate and measure value consistently, and you will use what you learn from strategic deployments to make that methodology sharper.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a quota-carrying role, nor is it a traditional advisory function. We are looking for a builder and a doer: someone who can engage credibly with senior customer stakeholders, get deep into a customer's operations and data, build rigorous models themselves, and turn ambiguous business problems into clear, actionable recommendations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will define how ElevenLabs understands, measures, and communicates customer value globally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In this role you will</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape value from the beginning.</strong> Partner with Revenue teams and prospects early in the sales cycle to understand customer priorities, identify high-value opportunities, and establish the business case for investing in ElevenLabs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build our global value strategy.</strong> Develop the frameworks, benchmarks, calculators, discovery approaches, and playbooks that define how ElevenLabs approaches value across industries and use cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale what works.</strong> Turn bespoke work with our largest customers into repeatable approaches that enable our Enterprise, Mid-Market, and Commercial teams to articulate and measure value without requiring bespoke support for every customer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Identify where ElevenLabs can have the greatest impact.</strong> Develop a deep understanding of a customer's business, workflows, economics, and strategic priorities to determine which use cases have the greatest potential and why.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Quantify the opportunity.</strong> Build rigorous financial and operational models that translate ElevenLabs use cases into measurable outcomes across revenue, cost, productivity, customer experience, and other relevant dimensions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define how value will be proven.</strong> Establish success metrics and measurement approaches for proofs of concept and deployments so that customers and ElevenLabs have a shared understanding of what success looks like from the outset.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measure value realization.</strong> Partner with customers and internal teams after deployment to understand the impact ElevenLabs is delivering, identify gaps between expected and realized value, and determine where additional opportunities exist.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support expansion and long-term customer value.</strong> Use insights from existing deployments to help customers understand what they have achieved and identify where ElevenLabs can drive additional impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work directly with the data.</strong> Analyze customer and industry data, build models, pressure-test assumptions, and develop recommendations yourself. You should be equally comfortable working in the details and communicating the implications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner with Deployment.</strong> On strategic accounts, work alongside Deployment Strategists who own the account-level business case, contributing methodology and capturing what works into reusable assets. Across the rest of the book, be the primary owner of value quantification and measurement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Influence senior stakeholders.</strong> Communicate complex analysis simply and credibly, and engage with senior leaders internally and externally when the opportunity requires it.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>10+ years of relevant experience</strong> across operating roles, strategy, management consulting, analytics, finance, customer strategy, or other roles requiring rigorous business problem solving.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong operating judgment.</strong> You understand how businesses work and can quickly get underneath a customer's operating model, workflows, economics, and strategic priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Exceptional analytical ability.</strong> You can personally build sophisticated financial and operational models, work with incomplete or imperfect information, make assumptions explicit, and turn analysis into decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Structured problem solving.</strong> You are comfortable starting with an ambiguous question such as "Where could AI create the most value in this business?" and developing a rigorous approach to answering it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer credibility.</strong> You can work directly with customers across functions and levels, ask incisive questions, challenge assumptions constructively, and establish trust quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial judgment.</strong> You understand how business value connects to technology investment decisions and can partner closely with Revenue teams while maintaining an objective, customer-first perspective.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellent communication.</strong> You can distill complex analysis into a clear point of view and communicate it effectively in writing and verbally, from working teams through senior executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A builder mentality.</strong> You are excited to start by doing the work yourself, learn from customers, and turn what works into scalable methodologies and tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity and pace.</strong> You can move quickly across industries, customer types, and use cases while maintaining a high bar for analytical rigor.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ability to operate globally.</strong> You are comfortable partnering with teams and customers across regions and traveling when valuable for customer work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Willingness to travel.</strong> Must be willing and able to travel up to 10% of the time.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus points</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in strategy or management consulting, particularly in operational transformation, technology, customer experience, or growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience as an operator within a technology company or other fast-moving business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working on AI, automation, customer experience, or technology-enabled business transformation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience developing business cases, value frameworks, or analytical methodologies that were ultimately scaled beyond an individual project or customer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with enterprise customers on complex, cross-functional initiatives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a global role within the Revenue organization. The role can be based in San Francisco or remotely, with the option to work from our San Francisco office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work with customers and ElevenLabs teams across regions and should expect travel for customer meetings and onsite work when it meaningfully advances the work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability or other legally protected statuses.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/elevenlabs/remote-value-strategist-187622","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1791664811},{"slug":"remote-enterprise-account-executive-ii-dach-180240","company_name":"Camunda","title":"Enterprise Account Executive II - DACH","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Camunda is <strong>the enterprise platform for agentic orchestration</strong>, enabling organizations to coordinate <strong>AI agents, people, and systems </strong>across complex, end-to-end business processes. With built-in governance, auditability, and human oversight, Camunda gives enterprises the control they need to move AI from pilots to production — safely and at scale. <strong>Trusted by over 700 organizations worldwide</strong>, including 9 of top 10 US banks, Camunda helps enterprises boost operational efficiency, accelerate time-to-value, and deliver better customer experiences.<br /><br /><strong>Fully remote and global,</strong> we are in the middle of something bigger: <strong>transforming into an AI-first organisation, built on our own platform</strong>. We use Agentic AI to automate, orchestrate intelligent processes, and elevate human contribution across every team.<br /><br />Named <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.gpbullhound.com/articles/top-100-next-unicorns-the-uk-france-and-germany-lead-with-the-most-promising-technology-companies-in-europe/"><u>GP Bullhound’s Top 100 Next Unicorn list,</u></a> <strong>2025 Great Place to Work certified.</strong> <em><strong>Visionary</strong></em><strong> </strong>in <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://page.camunda.com/wp-2025-gartner-magic-quadrant-for-boat"><strong><u>2025 Gartner® Magic Quadrant™</u></strong></a><strong> </strong>for Business Orchestration and Automation Technologies. ranked <strong>3rd in Flexa's 2026 </strong><a target="_blank" rel