ubsystems (propulsion, structures, avionics, GSE) are managed, dependencies tracked, and integration milestones owned</p><p>· Manage external dependencies: supplier lead times, test facility scheduling, regulatory submissions, and customer milestones</p><p>· Proactively flag scope creep, resource conflicts, and schedule risk to leadership – with options, not just problems</p><p>· Contribute to building the PM structure, tools, and ways of working for the department alongside team leads and fellow TPMs</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p>Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in aerospace, mechanical, systems, or a related engineering discipline</p><p>· 5–8 years in a hardware-heavy development environment; at least 2 in a project management, programme coordination, or technical lead role – career PMs without hardware exposure will not be considered</p><p>· Background in aerospace, defence, or a similarly regulated hardware domain; familiarity with vehicle-level or system-level development and qualification cycles is essential</p><p>· Experience managing cross-disciplinary programmes spanning multiple engineering domains (structures, propulsion, avionics, or similar) is a strong advantage</p><p>· Able to manage multiple concurrent projects across engineering, manufacturing, procurement, and testing</p><p>· Strong systems thinking – able to see the full picture, spot where the hard problems are likely to sit, and know when to dive into detail without losing the overall programme</p><p>· Strong planning skills – able to build a programme schedule from scratch, identify critical path, and keep it current</p><p>· Comfortable building structure in an ambiguous environment; pragmatic over bureaucratic</p><p>· Clear, direct communicator in English; German is an advantage</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/destinusgroup/technical-project-manager-efector-development