pany_name":"Destinusgroup","title":"System Integration Engineer (System Engineer - Effector Development)","description":"<p>The Destinus engineering team is seeking a Systems Engineer to lead the system-level definition and technical development of our effector programmes. This role sits at the centre of the development effort – bridging operational requirements and technical execution across propulsion, structures, avionics, and seeker.</p><p>The ideal candidate brings a defence systems background and understands the full development lifecycle of a guided effector – from ConOps and requirements through subsystem design, integration, and qualification. They are technically credible across multiple domains, rigorous in their systems thinking, and effective at driving alignment across disciplinary teams.</p><p><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p>· Define and own system-level requirements for effector programmes – capturing operational needs, translating them into technical requirements, and maintaining traceability from ConOps through to subsystem specifications</p><p>· Develop and maintain ConOps and operational scenario definitions; work with the customer and programme stakeholders to ensure operational intent is correctly reflected in the system design</p><p>· Define and manage technical interfaces between subsystems (propulsion, warhead/pyrotechnics, structures, avionics, guidance, and GSE); own the ICD and IRS documentation</p><p>· Lead trade studies and make-or-buy analyses to identify the best technical and commercial solutions at system and subsystem level</p><p>· Identify and track critical components and subsystems; define mitigation strategies for technical risk and drive resolution through the engineering team</p><p>· Lead or support system design reviews (SRR, PDR, CDR) and prepare the associated technical baseline documentation</p><p>· Coordinate system integration activities across propulsion, structures, avionics, and external teams; ensure interface