="min-height:1.5em">Are energized by having a lot of ownership and working closely with smart, mission-driven teammates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are able to work on-site from our Zurich office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus: You have legal domain familiarity, or experience in search and knowledge management, agentic search and data retrieval, or LegalTech – or you’ve worked in/with law firms, legal departments, or regulated industries<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you can look forward to:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A high-impact role in shaping a product and company with huge potential</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The chance to work on the cutting edge of long-horizon agentic AI, applied to real-world legal work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong, technical, and collaborative team that’s serious about building great software</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A culture that encourages experimentation, curiosity, and thoughtful decision-making</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Submit your application by October 16th. Our team will review all candidates after the closing date and reach out regarding next steps.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At DeepJudge, we believe great teams are built on diverse perspectives and experiences. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and are committed to fostering an inclusive, high-performance culture where everyone can thrive. We welcome applicants of all backgrounds and do not discriminate based on race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this role excites you, but you feel you don’t meet every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway and tell us why you’d be a great fit.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/deepjudge/agentic-product-manager-zurich-172987","tags":["Product & Design"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich HQ","created_at":1791535211},{"slug":"head-of-crypto-zurich-167809","company_name":"Satispay","title":"Head of Crypto","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Traditional banking has never really given people control over their financial life. Satispay exists to change that: to <strong>empower people through finance</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That means making financial services easy and accessible for millions of users. We started with payments, then benefits, investing, cards... and we’re not done. Not even close. Same logic every time: find a real problem, solve it properly, then look for the next one. The destination? To build the most loved financial platform in the world. Getting there takes leaders who own outcomes across teams, not just tasks, and set the tone for refusing the “someone else will fix this” culture. If that's how you lead, you'll fit right in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll be doing</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the Head of Crypto, you will be the driving force behind a brand new, core pillar of Satispay's expansion into the cryptocurrency and Web3 space. We already have a high-potential strategy in place—your mission is to take the reins, execute it flawlessly, adapt it when necessary, and expand upon it wherever possible.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Given the strategic importance of this initiative to Satispay, you will work with a high degree of autonomy and have direct, frequent touchpoints with the Satispay founding team to align on execution, team scaling, and long-term vision.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here’s what that looks like in practice:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hire &amp; Build Your Team:</strong> Identify talent needs, recruit, and structure a dedicated, high-performing cross-functional team from the ground up to bring Satispay's crypto vertical to life.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Execution &amp; Strategic Evolution:</strong> Take ownership of our existing crypto roadmap. Drive its execution to deliver immediate impact, while continuously evaluating the market to make necessary adjustments and expand our offerings when new opportunities arise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Executive Collaboration:</strong> Partner directly with the founders and C-level executives to ensure the crypto rollout continuously aligns with the company's ultimate mission to simplify everyday finance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Development:</strong> Oversee the end-to-end lifecycle of our crypto products—from infrastructure setup and go-to-market strategy to launch and continuous optimization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Regulatory Navigation:</strong> Work in lockstep with the Compliance and Legal teams to ensure all products align perfectly with evolving European regulations (such as MiCA) and safeguarding standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic Partnerships:</strong> Identify and establish crucial relationships with key players in the crypto ecosystem, including exchanges, custodians, liquidity providers, and blockchain networks.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will lead and mentor high-performing teams, collaborate closely with peers with structured communication and transparency, demonstrating a commitment to integrity and ownership.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are seeking for an execution-focused, and product-minded leader with a deep passion for digital assets that matches our company culture.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong> 7+ years of experience in crypto/Web3 initiatives at a regulated Fintech, exchange, or crypto-native company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Building:</strong> experience hiring, managing, and scaling specialized, high-performing teams in a fast-paced tech or financial environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Master of Execution:</strong> ability to take a high-level strategy and turn it into shipped products, scaling operations effectively from the ground up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Industry &amp; Market Expertise:</strong> Deep, technical understanding of blockchain architecture, crypto market dynamics, digital wallets, custody solutions, and Web3 infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Regulatory Awareness:</strong> Solid knowledge of the European crypto regulatory landscape (e.g., MiCA, AML/KYC for digital assets) and a history of launching products within a strict compliance framework.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic Adaptability:</strong> Ability to balance bold expansion with stringent risk management</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication &amp; Influence:</strong> Excellent ability to align internal and external stakeholders, translating complex crypto concepts into clear, actionable business updates for the founding team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Language Proficiency:</strong> You are completely fluent in English. Knowledge of Italian is considered a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We recognise that exceptional leadership comes in many forms. If you believe you have the vision, experience, and drive to help us shape the future of money, we encourage you to apply. We value the unique perspectives and strengths that exceptional leaders bring, even if their experience doesn't align with every listed requirement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why this is your place</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a unique opportunity to leverage your experience and leadership to make a profound impact on a company poised for significant future growth. We operate on a principle of reciprocity: significant strategic impacts are met with meaningful rewards and opportunities.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive transformative impact.</strong> Lead critical functions and initiatives that directly contribute to our mission and impact millions of users and businesses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operate in high-growth. </strong>Thrive in a dynamic, fast-moving environment that demands bravery, resilience, and rapid, decisive action at scale. Experience the excitement of navigating growth where change is constant and the customer base/services are rapidly expanding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Significant equity participation. </strong>Directly share in Satispay's success through a competitive Stock Option Plan designed to reward leadership and contribution to company growth and raise the bar for collective success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead exceptional teams. </strong>Build, mentor, and collaborate with high-performing teams in a culture of ownership, collective success, and continuous improvement fueled by feedback. You will learn from the best and lead alongside founders who are hands-on.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CareAbout: how we support your impact</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We move fast, and evolution never stops. It’s a fun ride, but it can be challenging. To make sure our people truly thrive, we’re committed to making their lives easier, both in the office and out in the world. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That’s why we created CareAbout:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">❤️ <strong>Health:</strong> private insurance for you and your family, psychological support with Serenis, mental health workshops.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 <strong>Financial resources:</strong> Stock Option Plan, meal vouchers, relocation support if you’re moving countries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">⚙️ <strong>Growth and development:</strong> professional development programs, internal mobility, language courses with Preply.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌱 <strong>Flexibility:</strong> unlimited PTO, hybrid working policy, flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">👨‍👩‍👧 <strong>Family:</strong> enhanced parental leave, additional leave for child sickness.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunity Employer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Satispay, we're proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and inclusion, welcoming individuals of all backgrounds. This opportunity is open to everyone, regardless - for instance - of race, colour, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, and national origin. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in a workplace where everyone belongs!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Learn more about us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious what it's actually like here? Our values and pillars shape how we work every day: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="ng-star-inserted" href="https://www.satispay.com/en-it/work-at-satispay/"><strong>explore them here</strong></a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-VR1</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-HYBRID</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>By submitting this application, I acknowledge that I have read and understood the content of the </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.satispay.com/en-it/legal-hub/privacy-policy/candidates/"><em>Privacy Policy</em></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/satispay/head-of-crypto-zurich-167809","tags":["Tech & Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1791535207},{"slug":"full-stack-software-engineer-zurich-403786","company_name":"Felfel","title":"Full Stack Software Engineer","description":"<br><strong>IN SHORT</strong><p><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Are you a versatile problem-solver who wants to write software that impacts the physical world? As a <strong>Full Stack Software Engineer</strong> (100%) in Zurich, you will be at the core of our operations, building systems that touch everything from warehouse automation to customer-facing smart fridges.</span></p><br><strong>YOUR RESPONSIBILITIES </strong><p><ul><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Take ownership of warehouse and supplier web apps used daily for inbound processing, picking, labeling, and inventory.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Develop and maintain our internal back-office tool, including the backend and GraphQL API that runs menus, deliveries, inventory, and customer sites.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Manage the service connecting automated picking lanes to the rest of the system to ensure uninterrupted warehouse operations.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Maintain and update the Point of Sale Android app running on hundreds of fridges, managing the release process for the entire fleet.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Integrate and support payment systems (Card, TWINT), our ERP, and other partner integrations.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Participate in the on-call rotation to debug live issues directly alongside the operations team.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Visit the warehouse on-site to test changes and gather feedback from the people actually using the software.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Translate vague problems from non-technical colleagues into shipped solutions without needing them broken down first.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Own production deployments, managing logs, alerts, and careful rollouts with clear rollback plans.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Break down larger features, review other engineers' pull requests, and proactively maintain system health through upgrades, testing, and cleanup.</li></ul></p><br><strong>YOUR PROFILE	</strong><p><ul><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Proven production experience in at least one typed backend language (such as C#, Java, Kotlin, Go, or TypeScript) and one modern frontend framework.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Track record of successfully owning software in production, including on-call duties, debugging from logs, and resolving live issues while users wait.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Familiarity with or willingness to dive into C#, TypeScript, Android, and Kotlin.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Prior exposure to hardware, IoT, edge devices, payments, logistics, retail operations, or Odoo environments is highly advantageous.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Demonstrated ability to dive into unfamiliar tech stacks, learn quickly, and ship reliable code.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Strong passion for collaborating directly with end-users, including warehouse and operations staff, rather than exclusively with other engineers.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);">High degree of curiosity and a proactive mindset to take full ownership of problems from end to end.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Fluent English communication skills (written and spoken); knowledge of German or French is a plus.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Non-smoker - we don't want you to smell like cigarettes, neither at work nor at customer meetings. After all, FELFEL is about good food.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Valid work permit or Swiss passport.</li></ul></p><br><strong>OUR BENEFITS</strong><p><ul><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Lots of delicious food, just a few steps away from your desk - we make your gastronomic dreams come true</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Best barista coffee and tea for the whole team, thanks to our innovative Gavetti coffee machine</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">5 weeks holiday per year, as well as the chance to buy an extra week of vacation </li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Two full weeks of ‘work from anywhere’ per year to bring more variety to your work day</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">We care about your future with an above-mandatory pension fund</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">New parents get 16 or 3 weeks, respectively, of fully paid parental leave. We also support the return to work by making a generous financial contribution to childcare until the child reaches kindergarten age.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">We encourage our employees to use public transport by covering your half-fare travelcard</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Great team events, such as our well-known FELFEL Summer Outing</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);">Stay active and healthy with our weekly sports sessions</li></ul><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);"> <br><strong>Does this sound like the job for you? We can't wait to learn more about you! APPLY NOW with your complete documents in either German or English.</strong></span></p><br><strong>ABOUT US</strong><p><span style="border:0px solid rgb(229,231,235);font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;text-transform:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);">FELFEL is all about good food and coffee in the workplace: we help Swiss employers become masters of hospitality. <br style="border:0px solid rgb(229,231,235);font-family:inherit;">With our smart fridge ‘FELFEL’ and delicious barista coffee ‘Gavetti’, we enable companies to provide their employees with first-class, ultra-fresh food and drinks throughout the day. Whether hearty and traditional, modern and vegan or high in protein - our weekly changing menu ensures that all employees always have something to be excited about ;).</span><span style="color:rgb(0,0,0);"><br></span><span style="border:0px solid rgb(229,231,235);font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;text-transform:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"><br style="border:0px solid rgb(229,231,235);font-family:inherit;">FELFEL is a family business that was founded in 2013. Today, we take care of around 1000 locations in Switzerland, and have 150 employees across our offices in Lausanne, Zurich and New York. </span><span style="color:rgb(0,0,0);"><br></span><span style="border:0px solid rgb(229,231,235);font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;text-transform:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"><br style="border:0px solid rgb(229,231,235);font-family:inherit;"></span><span style="color:rgb(0,0,0);"><a href="http://www.felfel.ch/" target="_blank" style="border:0px solid rgb(229,231,235);font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif, Inter, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-decoration:underline;color:rgb(66,66,66);font-weight:500;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;text-transform:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);" rel="noreferrer noopener"><span style="border:0px solid rgb(229,231,235);font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;">www.felfel.ch</span></a></span></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/felfel/full-stack-software-engineer-zurich-403786","tags":["Full-Stack Developer Zürich","Softwareentwickler Zürich","Kotlin Android Developer","Fullstack Entwickler","GraphQL","Logistics / Warehouse Software"],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1791533351},{"slug":"software-engineer-robot-autonomy-intern-zurich-308536","company_name":"Laelaps","title":"Software Engineer, Robot Autonomy, Intern","description":"<h1>Our Mission</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Laelaps AI, we believe robotics is entering a transformative decade, much like the arrival of the internet. Advances in AI, cloud computing, and hardware are reshaping what autonomous systems can do. Our mission is to build the intelligent software that powers physical security in the real world - enabling robots and sensors to handle dangerous and critical tasks that humans shouldn't have to. By engineering the orchestration layer for intelligent security, we aim to create a world that is safer, more secure, and more resilient.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a strong founding team based in Zurich, backed by visionary investors and advisors. We are engineering the future of security today!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Software Engineer intern on Robot Autonomy, you'll work on the software that runs on our legged security robots: how they perceive their surroundings, know where they are, and move through real customer sites on patrol. You'll join the team that owns everything on the robot and take a well-scoped problem from first experiment to a result that runs on hardware.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role focuses on building software for the robot autonomy stack that runs in the field. We'll agree your focus area with you during the interview process, based on your strengths and the team's priorities, and we expect you to own it from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is hands-on. You'll work with real sensor data and field logs, test on physical robots, and see first-hand why a robot that works in the lab can still fail on a live site at night, in rain, or after the layout changes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and improve components of the on-robot autonomy stack, such as perception, localisation and state estimation, or planning and navigation, depending on your background and the team's priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrate sensors such as lidar, cameras and IMU, and work with the data they produce in day, night and challenging weather.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reproduce issues from field deployments using logs and simulation, find the root cause, and help fix it at the right layer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design repeatable tests and clear metrics that show whether a change holds up across routes, lighting, weather and site layouts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test your work on physical robots, and join site visits to see how the system behaves in real operating conditions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply solid engineering practices: code review, version control, reproducible experiments and clear documentation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We're Looking For</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a strong robotics student who wants to see their work run on real robots, not only in simulation. You don't need every item below, but you should meet the core requirements and bring depth in at least one area of the autonomy stack. You'll join a small team that moves fast, expects ownership, and holds work to the standard of running on live customer sites.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Background</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Currently pursuing a Master's or PhD, or completed a Master's degree within the last year, in Robotics, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering or a closely related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated depth in at least one of perception, localisation and state estimation, or motion planning and navigation, through a thesis, research or a substantial project.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong coding skills in Python.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with ROS 2.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable using Linux, Docker and Git in your workflows.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with physical robots, ideally mobile or legged.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with lidar or camera processing, SLAM, or sensor fusion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with robotics simulators such as Isaac Sim, Gazebo or MuJoCo.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Publications or competition results in robotics (ICRA, IROS, RSS, CoRL).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What We Offer</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership: you are able to ship products and deliver project end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission: autonomous security that keeps people and critical sites safe, including in defence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Career path: a ground-floor seat with real runway. Prove your value and you will not have barriers to grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team: work directly with PhD-level co-founders in AI, Robotics, and Physics, alongside a strong (and fun) founding team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compensation: Competitive equity/salary package</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Culture: International founding team that is serious about building but does not take itself too seriously.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/laelaps/software-engineer-robot-autonomy-intern-zurich-308536","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zürich, Switzerland","crea