 you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>Key responsibilities</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Capture, define, and manage AIT and GSE requirements derived from vehicle, subsystem, manufacturing, and test needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and maintain key interfaces between flight hardware, GSE, tooling, test facilities, avionics, software, propulsion, and operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop system architectures, interface definitions, requirements specifications, verification matrices, and other supporting systems documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify requirements for tooling, fixtures, handling equipment, electrical and data connections, instrumentation, facilities, and test infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support vehicle integration, test planning, readiness reviews, procedure development, and the verification of AIT and GSE systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track system-level issues, interface actions, assumptions, and dependencies through to resolution in collaboration with the relevant technical teams.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>What we’re looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A degree in systems engineering, aerospace engineering, mechanical engineering, electrical engineering, or a related discipline; equivalent practical experience may also be relevant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in systems engineering, AIT, integration, test engineering, GSE, or another complex hardware-development environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience defining requirements, managing interfaces, and producing clear technical documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An understanding of how flight hardware, ground equipment, tooling, facilities, software, and 