chanical, manufacturing, and test teams to resolve cross-disciplinary issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support environmental testing, hardware campaigns, launch operations, and the continuous improvement of avionics designs and processes.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>What we are looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A degree in electrical engineering, electronics engineering, avionics, computer engineering, or a related discipline; equivalent practical experience may also be relevant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing, developing, testing, or integrating complex electronic hardware in aerospace, space, defence, automotive, robotics, or another high-reliability environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of analogue and digital electronics, power distribution, sensors, signal conditioning, and hardware interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience with schematics, PCB development, component selection, laboratory testing, and technical documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A methodical approach to requirements, verification, fault finding, configuration control, and hardware safety.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to work hands-on and independently while collaborating effectively across a small, fast-moving engineering team.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>Desirable experience</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flight hardware for launch vehicles, spacecraft, aircraft, missiles, or other safety-critical aerospace systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Electrical ground-support equipment, test stands, instrumentation, data acquisition, harnessing, or vehicle integration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embedded electronics, microcontrollers, commu