, system-level, and deployment-focused</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">. You will work at the intersection of hardware and software, ensuring that all onboard systems communicate reliably and perform in real operational environments. You will act as a </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">technical sparring partner</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> across avionics and system integration, contributing experience, pragmatism, and strong engineering judgment.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#121317">Your roadmap to make an impact</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Define and own the </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">end-to-end avionics architecture</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> for UAV platforms, from concept to operational deployment</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Define and implement system-level integration of </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">flight control (GNC), autonomy stacks, and C2 links</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Design and manage </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">onboard communication architectures</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> (e.g., MAVLink, DDS, Ethernet, CAN, serial protocols)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Integrate and validate </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">flight controllers, companion computers, sensors, radios, and payload systems</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Ensure </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">robust data flow, synchronization, and fault-tolerant behavior</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> across all subsystems</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Take avionics systems </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">from lab setup to real aircraft</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, ensuring reliable sim-to-real and bench-to-flight transition</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Lead and support </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) and system-level testing</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, including debugging complex integration issues</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Work closely with GNC, autonomy, C2, and EWIS/electrical teams to ensure </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">tight system coupling and clean interfaces</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Support </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">flight testing</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, including system bring-up, monitoring, logging, and post-flight analysis</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Define and implement </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">system monitoring, health checks, and fail-safe strategies</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Document system architectures, interfaces, and integration workflows in a </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">clear and maintainable way</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Support integration into </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">customer and operational environments</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, including Bundeswehr (Bw) requirements</span></p></li></ul> <br> <ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">5+ of hands-on experience in </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">avionics, robotics, or UAV system integration</span></strong></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong experience working with </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">real UAV systems</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, ideally across </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">fixed-wing and/or VTOL platforms</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Proven track record of </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">integrating complex systems</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> (fl