cial Sciences is an internationally active research institute and member of the Leibniz Association, funded by federal and state governments.</span><span style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;"><br> <br>Starting on<strong> 01.01.2027 </strong>our<strong> Department Data and Research on Society</strong>, <strong>Team Social Surveys</strong> located in <strong>Mannheim</strong>, is looking for a<br> <br><strong>Postdoctoral Researcher for Longitudinal Surveys (Salary group 13 TV-L, working time 100 %, Limitation for two years)</strong><br> <br></span><p style="line-height:115%;"><span style="line-height:115%;font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">Monitoring current social developments is a primary objective of the social sciences. The department </span><span style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;"><a href="https://www.gesis.org/en/institute/departments/data-and-research-on-society"><strong><span style="line-height:115%;color:rgb(0,112,192);">Data and Research on Society</span></strong></a></span><span style="line-height:115%;font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,112,192);font-size:15px;"> </span><span style="line-height:115%;font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">supports the social sciences in this task, by providing comprehensive data and tools to describe and analyse social changes. The department is responsible, among others for the implementation of the renowned European Social Survey (<a href="https://www.europeansocialsurvey.org/"><span style="color:#0070C0;"><strong>ESS</strong></span></a></span>) in Germany, and for the first time also for the collection of German data for the CROss-National Online Survey (<span style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;"><a href="https://www.europeansocialsurvey.org/methodology/methodological-research/modes-data-collection/cronos"><strong><span style="line-height:115%;color:rgb(0,112,192);">CRONOS</span></strong></