an a decade, we have supported companies through consulting, development, and training, delivering more than 1,000 successful projects for over 100 clients across almost all industries.<br><br>From AI strategy to implementation, we develop innovative solutions. With our expertise in AI Strategy, Generative AI, Agentic AI, Data &amp; AI Engineering, and AI Infrastructure, we support companies throughout their entire AI transformation.<br>Our mission: Creating value from Data &amp; AI.<br><br>Our AI Strategy team supports clients in designing and implementing their Data &amp; AI strategy. In doing so, we always aim to unlock the full potential of data, data science, and AI. Working closely with our clients, we address a wide range of strategic challenges, from the initial assessment of AI maturity and the formulation of Data &amp; AI strategies to the development and implementation of new operating models.</p><br><strong>Your tasks</strong><p>As a (Senior) Data Governance Consultant, you work at the intersection of <strong>business, technology and organization</strong>. You help our clients establish the <strong>ownership, processes and capabilities</strong> needed to make their data <strong>trustworthy, accessible and usable</strong>. From defining governance frameworks to embedding them in everyday operations, you enable organizations to create business value from data and AI.<br><ul><li>Assess clients’ <strong>data governance maturity</strong>, identify organizational and operational gaps, and develop actionable roadmaps aligned with their business and data strategies.</li><li>Design and implement <strong>data governance frameworks</strong>, including policies, standards, decision bodies and escalation processes.</li><li>Develop <strong>data governance operating models</strong> with clear roles and responsibilities for data owners, data stewards and cross-functional governance teams.</li><li>Help clients establish practical approaches to <strong>data quality management</strong>, including quality rules, monitoring, issue resolution and accountability.</li><li>Shape <strong>metadata management practices</strong>, including business glossaries, data catalogs and data lineage, to improve transparency and a shared understanding of data.</li><li>Translate <strong>governance requirements into processes and tooling needs</strong>, working closely with business stakeholders and technical experts from our development department.</li><li>Prepare and facilitate workshops, develop training and communication materials, and support the <strong>adoption of governance practices</strong> across business and IT teams.</li><li>Connect governance initiatives to <strong>data products and AI use cases</strong>, define measures of success, and communicate recommendations through clear, management-ready deliverables.</li></ul><strong>Additional responsibilities as Senior Data Governance Consultant: <br></strong><ul><li><strong>Lead data governance projects or major workstreams end-to-end</strong>, taking responsibility for scope, approach, deliverables, quality and stakeholder alignment.</li><li>Act as a <strong>trusted advisor to senior client stakeholders</strong> on data governance, ownership and operating model decisions.</li><li>Guide clients through <strong>organizational change</strong>, resolve competing stakeholder priorities and ensure governance practices become part of day-to-day operations.</li><li>Further develop our <strong>data governance methods, frameworks and service offerings</strong>, and contribute to business development through proposals and client discussions.</li><li><strong>Mentor junior colleagues</strong> and promote knowledge sharing on data governance and data management.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Your profile</strong><p><ul><li>Degree<strong> in data science, artificial intelligence, statistics, business or economics, computer science or business informatics, engineering</strong>, or a comparable quantitative, technolo