ars of relevant professional experience in full-time</strong>, with a clear focus on data governance or data management.</li><li>A <strong>proven track record of leading projects or substantial workstreams</strong> that put governance frameworks, roles and processes into practice.</li><li>Experience <strong>advising senior stakeholders</strong> on governance priorities, organizational responsibilities and implementation trade-offs.</li><li>Ability to define <strong>pragmatic governance approaches</strong> that fit a client’s maturity, business priorities and organizational structure.</li><li>Experience in <strong>business development</strong>, such as proposal work, developing service offerings or thought leadership, is a plus.</li><li>A <strong>high level of autonomy and confidence</strong> in representing our perspective on data governance in front of clients.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Our offer</strong><p><ul><li>Responsibility for shaping the service offering of a leading data &amp; AI consulting company in the DACH-region. </li><li>Comprehensive methodical and personal development opportunities, including regular internal and external training opportunities</li><li>Flat, team-based structures and a friendly work environment</li><li>Short decision routes and processes, as well as an agile work style</li><li>Performance-based attractive remuneration package</li><li>A modern and high-quality designed office</li><li>And many more perks such as Apple IT equipment (Macbook), remote work days, regular team events, company pension scheme, free drinks and snacks,…</li></ul><strong> </strong><br>We see diversity as essential and therefore welcome all applications – regardless of gender, nationality, ethnic and social background, religion/belief, disability, age sexual orientation and identity.</p><br><strong>Your application</strong><p>Apply now online!  Simply click on “apply online”, fill out the contact form and attach your current CV including a description of your so