ion-makers up to C-level on moving AI from pilot projects to genuine value creation: from strategy through the business case to implementation support. For technical depth, our Data &amp; AI Lab works alongside you, together bridging the gap from the strategic question to a working solution.</span></p><br><strong>Responsibilities</strong><p><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;">As part of our Consulting Team, you will take on the following:<br></span><ul><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;">Contributing to AI and digital strategies as well as the business models, portfolio and positioning strategies built on them</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;">Identifying, prioritizing and assessing AI use cases, including building robust business cases</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;">Independently running market, competitor, technology and best-practice analyses as the basis for strategic decisions</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;">Supporting implementation together with our Data &amp; AI Lab: you translate between business functions, management and development teams while keeping the tangible benefit in view</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;">Contributing to advisory work on the organizational prerequisites for successful AI adoption, such as governance, role models and capability building</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;">Preparing and presenting compelling decision papers and making complex topics accessible</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;">Owning your own workstreams within our project teams, including coordination with internal and external stakeholders</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:14px;">Confident client interaction at both expert and management leve